"repl-tasks.kfx: the REPL as FX-26 processes (C111), each entry running while
 the next is typed (docs/research/repl.md, stages 1 to 3), with nothing
 of it in Rust: what C103 did in kayak-fx26's Rust (two threads, keys
 read by a third, a refusal caught) done by FX-26's own processes,
 monitors and keys (C108, C109). C103's REPL, live-repl.kfx and its Rust,
 is kept beside this, behind kayak-fx26's `rust-repl` feature, to compare.

 Four kinds of task:
 - **The machine**, the program's own computation: the engine, whose
   heap is at `@h`, which no process may write, runs the entries by
   slices. A failure of a run is a value (C110), since nothing catches
   one here.
 - **The relay**, a process standing for the machine's mailbox, which the
   program's own computation has not: it keeps the front's requests until
   the machine asks for them, waiting or not.
 - **The front**, a process, its state in its own place: it reads the
   keys (`pselect`'s key arm), edits, checks and draws, and is told by the
   machine of each entry as it changes.
 - **Workers**, a process each, monitored: each check of the front's,
   whose refusal, a failure, is the worker's alone, and comes back as a
   value through its watcher (`worked`).

 The machine lowers and runs what the front checked: an entry given it
 was checked, and lowered, by a worker first, so the machine's lowering
 cannot fail. The draft is checked as it is typed (C96, C97), each try a
 worker's; a finished expression that only reads and allocates is run
 early by the machine, as the task in slot 0."

"What the program's own computation and the processes share: what
 crosses is copied (shared, in Rust), so it is data alone.

 To the machine (`asked`): an entry given, checked (its number, text,
 label, whether timed; what is written after its value, its definitions'
 lines, whether it only reads and allocates, the results it names); the
 draft to run early (its serial, text and type), or dropped; an entry
 cancelled; the step limit; in a scripted session, a round's end, and
 where to say what it ran; the front's end, or its failure (a bug).

 From it (`told`), to the front's mailbox: an entry as it is now (its
 number, state, line, the output since, when begun and ended, its steps,
 the collections meanwhile); the draft's run's outcome (its serial, its
 note, whether an error)."

"The effects of the REPL's tasks (C111): a worker's waiting for its outcome;
 the machine's, the engine's and the relay's I-cells; the front's, keys,
 the screen, files, the workers, the relay; the whole session's."
(define-effect working (maxeff (alloc @q) (alloc @w) (init @q) (await @q) (send @q) nondet spin))
(define-effect machining (maxeff running (io terminal) (alloc @m) (send @m) (await @m) (send @f) (init @q) nondet))
(define-effect fronting (maxeff kfx nondet (io stdout) (io stderr) (io stdin) (io clock) (io fs-read) (io fs-write) (io terminal) (alloc @q) (alloc @w) (init @q) (await @q) (send @q) (send @m)))
(define-effect front-loop (maxeff fronting (alloc @q) (init @q) (await @q)))
(define-effect repling (maxeff machining fronting (init @m) (alloc @f) (alloc @io) (read @io) (send @m) (receive @m)))

(define tasks
  (module
    (hide
      (define-datatype told
        (entry-told i64 i64 string string i64 i64 i64 i64)
        (draft-told i64 string bool))

      "A scripted round's outcome: the news, the clock after the slices, and
       whether no task may run."
      (define-datatype ran (ran (listof told acyclic) i64 bool))

      (define-datatype asked
        (entry-asked i64 string string bool string string bool (listof i64 acyclic))
        (draft-asked i64 string string)
        (draft-unasked)
        (cancel-asked i64)
        (limit-asked i64)
        (round-ended i64 (icell ran @q))
        (front-ended)
        (front-failed string))

      "The relay's mailbox: a request from the front; the machine asking for
       those kept, into an I-cell, waiting for one or not."
      (define-datatype relayed
        (from-front asked)
        (taken (icell (listof asked acyclic) @m) bool))

      "Entries' states, as each side keeps them."
      (define st-checking i64 0)
      (define st-waiting i64 1)
      (define st-running i64 2)
      (define st-done i64 3)
      (define st-failed i64 4)
      (define st-interrupted i64 5)
      (define st-refused i64 6)

      "Text, drawing, history and commands: the helpers C103's REPL has,
       the same (live-repl.kfx)."

      (define seconds (subr kfx (i64) string)
        (lambda (ms)
          (string-append (i64->string (i64-quotient ms 1000))
                         (string-append "." (string-append (i64->string (i64-quotient (i64-remainder ms 1000) 100)) " s")))))

      (define spinner (subr kfx (i64) string)
        (lambda (now)
          (let ((frames "⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏"))
            (char->string (string-ref-i64 frames (i64-remainder (i64-quotient now 80) 10))))))

      (define clamped (subr kfx (i64 i64) i64)
        (lambda (i n) (cond ((i64< i 0) 0) ((i64> i n) n) (else i))))

      (define cut (subr kfx (string i64 i64) string)
        (lambda (s from to)
          (let ((n (string-length-i64 s)))
            (substring s (i64->int (clamped from n)) (i64->int (clamped to n))))))

      (define-rec
        (line-start (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
          (lambda (s i) (if (or (i64<= i 0) (char=? (string-ref-i64 s (i64- i 1)) #\newline)) i (line-start s (i64- i 1))))))

      (define-rec
        (line-end (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
          (lambda (s i) (if (or (i64>= i (string-length-i64 s)) (char=? (string-ref-i64 s i) #\newline)) i (line-end s (i64+ i 1))))))

      (define name-char? (subr kfx (char) bool)
        (lambda (c) (not (or (char-whitespace? c) (char=? c #\() (char=? c #\)) (char=? c #\") (char=? c #\')))))

      (define-rec
        (spaces-start (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
          (lambda (s i) (if (and (i64> i 0) (char-whitespace? (string-ref-i64 s (i64- i 1)))) (spaces-start s (i64- i 1)) i))))

      (define word-start (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
        (lambda (s i)
          "Where ^W deletes back to: past spaces, then a name, or one other character."
          (let ((j (spaces-start s i)))
            (cond ((and (i64> j 0) (name-char? (string-ref-i64 s (i64- j 1)))) (name-start s j))
                  ((and (i64> j 0) (i64= j i)) (i64- j 1))
                  (else j)))))

      (define-rec
        (name-start (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
          (lambda (s i) (if (and (i64> i 0) (name-char? (string-ref-i64 s (i64- i 1)))) (name-start s (i64- i 1)) i))))

      (define column-on (subr kfx (string i64 i64) i64)
        (lambda (d start col)
          "The index `col` along the line beginning at `start`, or its end."
          (let ((end (line-end d start))) (if (i64< (i64+ start col) end) (i64+ start col) end))))

      (define-rec
        (nth-string (subr kfx (strings i64) string)
          (lambda (xs i) (cond ((null? xs) "") ((i64= i 0) (car xs)) (else (nth-string (cdr xs) (i64- i 1)))))))

      (define-rec
        (trimmed-start (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic)) (listof char acyclic))
          (lambda (cs) (if (and (not (null? cs)) (char-whitespace? (car cs))) (trimmed-start (cdr cs)) cs))))

      (define trimmed-end (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (s) (list->string (oldest-first-chars (trimmed-start (oldest-first-chars (string-chars s) nil)) nil))))

      (define-rec
        (oldest-first-chars (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) (listof char acyclic)) (listof char acyclic))
          (lambda (cs acc) (if (null? cs) acc (oldest-first-chars (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc))))))

      (define-rec
        (escaped (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) chars) chars)
          (lambda (cs acc)
            (cond ((null? cs) acc)
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) (escaped (cdr cs) (put "\\n" acc)))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\\) (escaped (cdr cs) (put "\\\\" acc)))
                  (else (escaped (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc)))))))

      (define-rec
        (unescaped (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) chars) chars)
          (lambda (cs acc)
            (cond ((null? cs) acc)
                  ((and (char=? (car cs) #\\) (not (null? (cdr cs))))
                   (unescaped (cdr (cdr cs)) (cons (if (char=? (car (cdr cs)) #\n) #\newline (car (cdr cs))) acc)))
                  (else (unescaped (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc)))))))

      (define-rec
        (history-text (subr kfx (strings i64 chars) chars)
          (lambda (hs n acc)
            "The history, oldest first, `n` entries at most, as the file has it."
            (if (or (null? hs) (i64<= n 0))
                acc
                (put "\n" (escaped (string-chars (car hs)) (history-text (cdr hs) (i64- n 1) acc)))))))

      (define-rec
        (common-prefix (subr kfx (string strings) string)
          (lambda (p xs)
            (cond ((null? xs) p)
                  ((has-prefix? (car xs) p) (common-prefix p (cdr xs)))
                  (else (common-prefix (substring p 0 (i64->int (i64- (string-length-i64 p) 1))) xs))))))

      (define-rec
        (deduped-names (subr kfx (strings strings) strings)
          (lambda (xs seen)
            (cond ((null? xs) nil)
                  ((string-member? (car xs) seen) (deduped-names (cdr xs) seen))
                  (else (cons (car xs) (deduped-names (cdr xs) (cons (car xs) seen))))))))

      (define-rec
        (words-of-at-most (subr kfx (strings i64) string)
          (lambda (xs n)
            (cond ((null? xs) "")
                  ((i64= n 0) "…")
                  ((null? (cdr xs)) (car xs))
                  (else (string-append (car xs) (string-append " " (words-of-at-most (cdr xs) (i64- n 1)))))))))

      (define help-text string
        ",help              this; ,help NAME: what NAME is
,type E            E's type and effect, checked and not run
,time E            E run, then its time, steps and collections
,load FILE         FILE's forms, an entry
,pending           the entries not ended
,cancel K          entry K interrupted (^C: the newest)
,step-limit [N|none]  how many steps an entry may take
,apropos TEXT      the names containing TEXT
,quit              leave now (^D: when every entry has ended)
Anything else is forms, checked and run as an entry; %K is entry K's value;
an entry naming one that has not ended waits for it.")

      (define command-whole? (subr kfx (string) bool)
        (lambda (line)
          "Whether a command's line is whole: its forms, if any, closed."
          (let ((rest (command-rest line)))
            (or (null? (trimmed-start (string-chars rest))) (repl-complete? rest)))))

      (define-rec
        (word-end (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64) i64)
          (lambda (cs i) (if (or (null? cs) (char-whitespace? (car cs))) i (word-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1))))))

      (define command-word (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (line) (substring line 0 (i64->int (word-end (string-chars line) 0)))))

      (define command-rest (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (line)
          (let ((n (word-end (string-chars line) 0)))
            (list->string (trimmed-start (string-chars (substring line (i64->int n) (i64->int (string-length-i64 line)))))))))

      (define-rec
        (words-lines (subr kfx (strings) string)
          (lambda (xs) (cond ((null? xs) "") ((null? (cdr xs)) (car xs)) (else (string-append (car xs) (string-append "\n" (words-lines (cdr xs)))))))))

      (define first-line (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (s) (let ((ls (lines-of (string-chars s) nil nil))) (if (null? ls) "" (car ls)))))

      (define-rec
        (wrapped-rows (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 i64 i64) i64)
          (lambda (cs col width n)
            "The rows text takes, starting at `col`, its lines wrapped at `width`."
            (cond ((null? cs) n)
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) (wrapped-rows (cdr cs) 7 width (i64+ n 1)))
                  ((i64>= col width) (wrapped-rows (cdr cs) 1 width (i64+ n 1)))
                  (else (wrapped-rows (cdr cs) (i64+ col 1) width n))))))

      (define-rec
        (prompted (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 i64 i64 chars) chars)
          (lambda (cs i from to acc)
            "The draft as drawn: each line after the first after `     | `; the
             characters `from` to `to` underlined, a subform a refusal is about."
            (let ((marked (cond ((i64>= from to) acc)
                                ((i64= i from) (put "\x1b;[4m" acc))
                                ((i64= i to) (put "\x1b;[24m" acc))
                                (else acc))))
              (cond ((null? cs) marked)
                    ((char=? (car cs) #\newline)
                     (prompted (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) from to
                               (if (and (i64>= i from) (i64< i to))
                                   (put "\x1b;[4m" (put "\r\n     | " (put "\x1b;[24m" marked)))
                                   (put "\r\n     | " marked))))
                    (else (prompted (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) from to (cons (car cs) marked))))))))

      (define-rec
        (column-after (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 i64) i64)
          (lambda (cs col width)
            "The column text leaves the cursor at, wrapped as `wrapped-rows` wraps it."
            (cond ((null? cs) col)
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) (column-after (cdr cs) 7 width))
                  ((i64>= col width) (column-after (cdr cs) 1 width))
                  (else (column-after (cdr cs) (i64+ col 1) width))))))

      (define-rec
        (lines-of (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) chars strings) strings)
          (lambda (cs acc out)
            "Text's lines, the last, if not ended by a newline, too."
            (cond ((null? cs) (if (null? acc) (oldest-first-strings out nil) (oldest-first-strings (cons (rev->string acc) out) nil)))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) (lines-of (cdr cs) nil (cons (rev->string acc) out)))
                  (else (lines-of (cdr cs) (cons (car cs) acc) out))))))

      (define-rec
        (oldest-first-strings (subr kfx (strings strings) strings)
          (lambda (xs acc) (if (null? xs) acc (oldest-first-strings (cdr xs) (cons (car xs) acc))))))

      (define-datatype closing (unclosable) (closed-as string i64 (listof i64 acyclic) bool))

      (define-datatype scan (ill-balanced) (scanned-as (listof i64 acyclic) bool))

      (define-rec
        (kept-end (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 i64 bool i64) i64)
          (lambda (cs i str comment atom)
            "Where the text stops being finished: at a string not closed (begun
             at `str`), or a name, number or character running to the end (begun
             at `atom`); -1 for none."
            (cond ((null? cs) (cond ((i64>= str 0) str) ((i64>= atom 0) atom) (else i)))
                  ((i64>= str 0)
                   (cond ((char=? (car cs) #\\) (if (null? (cdr cs)) str (kept-end (cdr (cdr cs)) (i64+ i 2) str #f -1)))
                         ((char=? (car cs) #\") (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) -1 #f -1))
                         (else (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) str #f -1))))
                  (comment (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) -1 (not (char=? (car cs) #\newline)) -1))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\") (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) i #f -1))
                  ((i64= (char->i64 (car cs)) 59) (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) -1 #t -1))
                  ((and (char=? (car cs) #\#) (not (null? (cdr cs))) (char=? (car (cdr cs)) #\\))
                   (let ((from (if (i64>= atom 0) atom i)))
                     (if (null? (cdr (cdr cs))) from (kept-end (cdr (cdr (cdr cs))) (i64+ i 3) -1 #f from))))
                  ((name-char? (car cs)) (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) -1 #f (if (i64>= atom 0) atom i)))
                  (else (kept-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) -1 #f -1))))))

      (define-rec
        (before-quotes (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
          (lambda (s i)
            "`i`, less the quotes before it, which wait for a datum."
            (if (and (i64> i 0) (i64= (char->i64 (string-ref-i64 s (i64- i 1))) 39)) (before-quotes s (i64- i 1)) i))))

      (define-rec
        (open-lists (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 (listof i64 acyclic) bool bool) scan)
          (lambda (cs i open str comment)
            "Where the lists still open begin, the innermost first; and whether the
             text ends in a comment. A list closed that was never opened: none."
            (cond ((null? cs) (scanned-as open comment))
                  (str
                   (cond ((char=? (car cs) #\\) (if (null? (cdr cs)) (scanned-as open #f) (open-lists (cdr (cdr cs)) (i64+ i 2) open #t #f)))
                         ((char=? (car cs) #\") (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) open #f #f))
                         (else (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) open #t #f))))
                  (comment (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) open #f (not (char=? (car cs) #\newline))))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\") (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) open #t #f))
                  ((i64= (char->i64 (car cs)) 59) (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) open #f #t))
                  ((and (char=? (car cs) #\#) (not (null? (cdr cs))) (char=? (car (cdr cs)) #\\) (not (null? (cdr (cdr cs)))))
                   (open-lists (cdr (cdr (cdr cs))) (i64+ i 3) open #f #f))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\() (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) (cons i open) #f #f))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\)) (if (null? open) (ill-balanced) (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) (cdr open) #f #f)))
                  (else (open-lists (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) open #f #f))))))

      (define-rec
        (closers (subr kfx (i64) string)
          (lambda (n) (if (i64<= n 0) "" (string-append ")" (closers (i64- n 1)))))))

      (define closed-text (subr kfx (string) closing)
        (lambda (text)
          "The draft closed off: what was typed, less a token still being typed,
           its lists closed; where that stops being the draft, the lists it
           closed, and whether the draft was finished (nothing left out or
           closed)."
          (let* ((kept (before-quotes text (kept-end (string-chars text) 0 -1 #f -1)))
                 (typed (cut text 0 kept)))
            (tagcase (open-lists (string-chars typed) 0 nil #f #f)
              (ill-balanced () (unclosable))
              (scanned-as (open comment)
                (closed-as (string-append typed (string-append (if (and comment (not (null? open))) "\n" "") (closers (size open))))
                            kept open
                            (and (null? open) (i64= kept (string-length-i64 text)))))))))

      (define-rec
        (i64-member? (subr kfx (i64 (listof i64 acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (x xs) (cond ((null? xs) #f) ((i64= x (car xs)) #t) (else (i64-member? x (cdr xs)))))))

      (define-rec
        (quoted-at? (subr kfx (string i64) bool)
          (lambda (s i)
            "Whether the list at `i` is quoted data: a quote before it."
            (cond ((i64<= i 0) #f)
                  ((char-whitespace? (string-ref-i64 s (i64- i 1))) (quoted-at? s (i64- i 1)))
                  (else (i64= (char->i64 (string-ref-i64 s (i64- i 1))) 39))))))

      (define-rec
        (list-end (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64 i64 bool bool) i64)
          (lambda (cs i depth str comment)
            "Where the list begun at the first of `cs` (at `i`) ends, past its
             close; or the text's end."
            (cond ((null? cs) i)
                  (str
                   (cond ((char=? (car cs) #\\) (if (null? (cdr cs)) (i64+ i 1) (list-end (cdr (cdr cs)) (i64+ i 2) depth #t #f)))
                         ((char=? (car cs) #\") (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) depth #f #f))
                         (else (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) depth #t #f))))
                  (comment (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) depth #f (not (char=? (car cs) #\newline))))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\") (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) depth #t #f))
                  ((i64= (char->i64 (car cs)) 59) (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) depth #f #t))
                  ((and (char=? (car cs) #\#) (not (null? (cdr cs))) (char=? (car (cdr cs)) #\\) (not (null? (cdr (cdr cs)))))
                   (list-end (cdr (cdr (cdr cs))) (i64+ i 3) depth #f #f))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\() (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) (i64+ depth 1) #f #f))
                  ((char=? (car cs) #\)) (if (i64<= depth 1) (i64+ i 1) (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) (i64- depth 1) #f #f)))
                  (else (list-end (cdr cs) (i64+ i 1) depth #f #f))))))

      (define-rec
        (name-end (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
          (lambda (s i) (if (and (i64< i (string-length-i64 s)) (name-char? (string-ref-i64 s i))) (name-end s (i64+ i 1)) i))))

      (define datum-end (subr kfx (string i64) i64)
        (lambda (s at)
          "Where the datum written at `at` ends: a list at its close, a string at
           its quote, a name or number at the delimiter after it."
          (cond ((i64>= at (string-length-i64 s)) at)
                ((or (char=? (string-ref-i64 s at) #\() (char=? (string-ref-i64 s at) #\"))
                 (list-end (string-chars (cut s at (string-length-i64 s))) at 0 #f #f))
                (else (name-end s (i64+ at 1))))))

      (define-rec
        (closers-filled (subr kfx (i64 i64 i64) string)
          (lambda (i n filled)
            "The closers of `n` open lists from the innermost (`i` 0), a filler
             before each if `filled` is -1, else before list `filled`'s alone."
            (if (i64>= i n)
                ""
                (string-append (if (or (i64= filled -1) (i64= filled i)) " %fill)" ")") (closers-filled (i64+ i 1) n filled))))))

      (define-rec
        (each-filled (subr kfx (string i64 i64) strings)
          (lambda (text i n)
            "`text` closed with a filler in list `i` alone, for each list around
             the innermost."
            (if (i64>= i n) nil (cons (string-append text (closers-filled 0 n i)) (each-filled text (i64+ i 1) n))))))

      (define refused-offset (subr kfx (string) i64)
        (lambda (m)
          "Where in the draft a refusal is, as `refuse` says it for one, or -1."
          (let ((p "kfx: <draft>@"))
            (if (has-prefix? m p)
                (number-from (digits-of (string-chars (cut m (string-length-i64 p) (string-length-i64 m)))) 0)
                -1))))

      (define-rec
        (digits-of (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic)) (listof char acyclic))
          (lambda (cs) (if (and (not (null? cs)) (char-numeric? (car cs))) (cons (car cs) (digits-of (cdr cs))) nil))))

      (define without-prefix (subr kfx (string string) string)
        (lambda (s p) (if (has-prefix? s p) (cut s (string-length-i64 p) (string-length-i64 s)) s)))

      (define refusal-words (subr kfx (string) string)
        (lambda (m)
          "A refusal of the draft without where: what it is."
          (cond ((has-prefix? m "kfx: <draft>@")
                 (let ((at (int->i64 (string-search m ": " 13))))
                   (if (i64< at 0) m (without-prefix (cut m (i64+ at 2) (string-length-i64 m)) "in a top-level expression: "))))
                ((has-prefix? m "kfx: ") (without-prefix (cut m 5 (string-length-i64 m)) "in a top-level expression: "))
                (else m))))

      (define-rec
        (number-from (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64) i64)
          (lambda (cs n) (if (null? cs) n (number-from (cdr cs) (i64+ (i64* n 10) (i64- (char->i64 (car cs)) 48)))))))

      (define definition-form? (subr kfx (sexp) bool)
        (lambda (f)
          (any? (lambda ((h string)) (head-is? f h))
                (list "define" "define*" "define-rec" "define-type" "define-datatype" "define-generative" "define-effect"))))

      (define-rec
        (named-results (subr kfx (sexp) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (x)
            (tagcase x
              (sym (n f p)
                (let ((cs (string-chars n)))
                  (if (and (not (null? cs)) (char=? (car cs) #\%) (not (null? (cdr cs)))
                           (not (any? (lambda ((c char)) (not (char-numeric? c))) (cdr cs))))
                      (list (number-from (cdr cs) 0))
                      nil)))
              (lst (xs f l p) (concat (map named-results xs)))
              (else other nil)))))

      (define quiet-effect? (subr kfx (strings) bool)
        (lambda (es)
          "Whether an effect only reads globals, allocates, and spins: an entry
           with it runs beside others."
          (not (any? (lambda ((a string))
                       (not (or (string=? a "spin") (string=? a "@globals") (has-prefix? a "g:")
                                (has-prefix? a "read:") (has-prefix? a "alloc:"))))
                     es))))

      (define loud-atoms (subr kfx (strings) strings)
        (lambda (es)
          "The atoms of an effect that keep an entry from running beside others."
          (concat (map (lambda ((a string)) (if (quiet-effect? (list a)) nil (list a))) es))))

      (define-rec
        (reversed-onto (poly ((a type)) (subr kfx ((listof a acyclic) (listof a acyclic)) (listof a acyclic)))
          (lambda (xs acc) (if (null? xs) acc (reversed-onto (cdr xs) (cons (car xs) acc))))))


      (define-rec
        (count-newlines (subr kfx ((listof char acyclic) i64) i64)
          (lambda (cs n) (cond ((null? cs) n) ((char=? (car cs) #\newline) (count-newlines (cdr cs) (i64+ n 1))) (else (count-newlines (cdr cs) n))))))


      "Checks, each a worker's (C111). The checker refuses by failing, which
       in a monitored process fails that process alone: its watcher is sent
       the refusal, which comes back as a value. A job: an entry's forms (the
       checker's environment and the globals' names before it, its number,
       text and label); `,type`'s text; a try of the draft, or of a text with
       a hole in it, finished or not. What is found, or the refusal."
      (define-datatype job
        (check-entry cv strings i64 string string)
        (type-of cv string)
        (try cv strings string bool)
        (hole-items string))

      (define-datatype done
        (entry-done cv strings string string bool (listof i64 acyclic))
        (shown-done string)
        (tried-none)
        (tried-expression string strings (listof i64 acyclic))
        (tried-definitions string)
        (items-done i64 string)
        (refused-done string))

      (define result-bound (subr kfx (cv sexp string) cv)
        (lambda (v form name)
          "The checker's environment with `name` a global of `form`'s type."
          (tagcase (with expressions (synth (at v "a top-level expression" nil) (new-state) form))
            (res (t es s) (with-binds v (list (global v name (scheme nil (zonk s t)))))))))

      (define expression-effects (subr kfx (cv sexp) strings)
        (lambda (v form)
          (tagcase (with expressions (synth (at v "a top-level expression" nil) (new-state) form))
            (res (t es s) es))))

      (define-rec
        (checked-all (subr kfx (cv sexps) cv)
          (lambda (v forms) (if (null? forms) v (checked-all (checked-form v (car forms)) (cdr forms))))))

      (define-rec
        (definition-lines (subr kfx (cv sexps) strings)
          (lambda (v forms)
            "What the REPL writes of each definition among `forms`."
            (cond ((null? forms) nil)
                  ((definition-form? (car forms))
                   (let ((l (form-type v (car forms))))
                     (if (string=? l "") (definition-lines v (cdr forms)) (cons l (definition-lines v (cdr forms))))))
                  (else (definition-lines v (cdr forms)))))))

      (define-rec
        (entry-checked (subr kfx (cv strings i64 sexps string string bool (listof i64 acyclic)) done)
          (lambda (v gs k forms typed defined quiet needs)
            "Each form checked, in order, as C103's `entry-forms` did, and
             lowered, as the machine will lower it, so that its lowering fails
             here if anywhere: an expression's value `%k`'s, the global bound
             at its type; what is written after its value, the lines of the
             definitions, whether it only reads and allocates."
            (if (null? forms)
                (entry-done v gs typed defined quiet needs)
                (let* ((form (car forms))
                       (expression (not (definition-form? form)))
                       (shown-type (if expression (form-type v form) ""))
                       (effects (if expression (expression-effects v form) nil))
                       (name (string-append "%" (i64->string k)))
                       (checked (checked-form v form))
                       (v2 (if expression (result-bound checked form name) checked))
                       (gs2 (onto gs (new-names (if expression (list name) (global-names (list form))) gs)))
                       (line (if expression shown-type (form-type v2 form))))
                  (begin
                    (lower-tops (list form) gs2)
                    (entry-checked v2 gs2 k (cdr forms)
                                   (if expression line typed)
                                   (cond ((or expression (string=? line "")) defined)
                                         ((string=? defined "") line)
                                         (else (string-append defined (string-append "\n" line))))
                                   (and quiet expression (quiet-effect? effects))
                                   needs)))))))

      (define* job-done (subr kfx (job) done)
        (lambda (j)
          (tagcase j
            (check-entry (v gs k text label)
              (let ((forms (read-all (string-chars text) (if (string=? label "") (string-append "<fx26:" (string-append (i64->string k) ">")) label) 1)))
                (entry-checked v gs k forms "" "" #t (concat (map named-results forms)))))
            (type-of (v text)
              (let ((forms (read-all (string-chars text) "<,type>" 1)))
                (if (null? forms) (begin (error "nothing to type") (shown-done "")) (shown-done (form-type v (car forms))))))
            (try (v gs text finished)
              ;; Checked after what the entries before it defined; if finished,
              ;; an expression's type and effect found, and it lowered, as the
              ;; machine will lower it to run it early; definitions' lines.
              (let* ((forms (read-all (string-chars text) "<draft>" 1))
                     (v2 (checked-all v forms)))
                (cond ((or (not finished) (null? forms)) (tried-none))
                      ((and (null? (cdr forms)) (not (definition-form? (car forms))))
                       (begin
                         (lower-tops (list (car forms)) gs)
                         (tried-expression (form-type v (car forms)) (expression-effects v (car forms)) (named-results (car forms)))))
                      (else (tried-definitions (words-lines (definition-lines v2 forms)))))))
            (hole-items (text)
              ;; The innermost open list's items so far, read: how many, and its
              ;; operator, if a name.
              (let* ((inner (read-all (string-chars text) "<hint>" 1))
                     (xs (if (null? inner) nil (items (car inner)))))
                (items-done (size xs) (if (null? xs) "" (tagcase (car xs) (sym (op f p) (if (keyword? op) "" op)) (else other "")))))))))

      (define* refusal (subr pure (string) done) (lambda (m) (refused-done m)))


      (define* worked (subr working (job) done)
        (lambda (j)
          "`j` done by a worker, whose watcher, a relay of one message, puts
           what it is sent, the outcome or the refusal, where this waits."
          (let* ((out (the (icell done @q) (make-icell)))
                 (relay (the (addr done @q) (spawn (box done r) (icell-put! out (receive box))))))
            (begin
              (the (addr unit @w) (spawn-monitored relay refusal (box unit r) (send relay (job-done j))))
              (icell-get out)))))


      "The machine (C111): the program's own computation, at `@h`, as the
       engine is. An entry: its number; what the front found (what is written
       after its value, its definitions' lines, whether it only reads and
       allocates, the results it names); and what changes: its state, its
       tops to run (main.kfx's numbers), its value as written, its output not
       yet told, when it began and ended, what was last told of it; whether
       `,time` asked for its steps and collections, its steps so far, and the
       collections before and after it."
      (define-type mentry
        (productof (num i64) (typed string) (defined string) (quiet bool) (needs (listof i64 acyclic))
                   (state (ref i64 @h)) (tops (ref (listof i64 acyclic) @h)) (shown (ref string @h))
                   (out (ref string @h)) (began (ref i64 @h)) (ended (ref i64 @h)) (drawn (ref string @h))
                   (timed bool) (steps (ref i64 @h)) (gcs i64) (gcs-after (ref i64 @h))))

      "The machine's session: its entries, the newest first; whether live;
       the entry run last (for turns); the steps an entry may take; a slice's
       steps and time; the news not yet sent, the newest first; the draft's
       run (its state, 0 none, 1 running in slot 0, 2 ended; serial; type;
       the IR tables' lengths before it was numbered; its steps); whether the
       front has ended."
      (define m-entries (ref (listof mentry acyclic) @h) (new nil))
      (define m-live (ref bool @h) (new #f))
      (define m-last-run (ref i64 @h) (new 0))
      (define m-step-limit (ref i64 @h) (new -1))
      (define slice-steps i64 20000)
      (define m-slice-ns (ref i64 @h) (new -1))
      (define m-news (ref (listof told acyclic) @h) (new nil))
      (define m-spec-state (ref i64 @h) (new 0))
      (define m-spec-serial (ref i64 @h) (new 0))
      (define m-spec-type (ref string @h) (new ""))
      (define m-spec-marks (ref (listof i64 acyclic) @h) (new nil))
      (define m-spec-steps (ref i64 @h) (new 0))
      (define spec-limit i64 2000000)
      (define m-over (ref bool @h) (new #f))

      (define m-made (subr running (i64 string string bool (listof i64 acyclic) i64 (listof i64 acyclic) string bool i64) mentry)
        (lambda (k typed defined quiet needs state tops shown timed now)
          (product (num k) (typed typed) (defined defined) (quiet quiet) (needs needs)
                   (state (new state)) (tops (new tops)) (shown (new shown)) (out (new ""))
                   (began (new now)) (ended (new (if (i64= state st-done) now -1))) (drawn (new ""))
                   (timed timed) (steps (new 0)) (gcs (get collections)) (gcs-after (new -1)))))

      (define m-ended! (subr running (mentry i64 i64) unit)
        (lambda (e state now)
          "An entry ended, in `state`: when, and the collections so far."
          (begin
            (set (extract e state) state)
            (set (extract e ended) now)
            (set (extract e gcs-after) (get collections)))))

      (define m-unfinished? (subr running (mentry) bool)
        (lambda (e)
          (let ((s (get (extract e state))))
            (or (i64= s st-checking) (i64= s st-waiting) (i64= s st-running)))))

      (define-rec
        (m-numbered (subr running ((listof mentry acyclic) i64) (listof mentry acyclic))
          (lambda (es k)
            (cond ((null? es) nil)
                  ((i64= (extract (car es) num) k) (list (car es)))
                  (else (m-numbered (cdr es) k))))))

      (define-rec
        (m-oldest-first (subr kfx ((listof mentry acyclic) (listof mentry acyclic)) (listof mentry acyclic))
          (lambda (es acc) (if (null? es) acc (m-oldest-first (cdr es) (cons (car es) acc))))))

      (define-rec
        (m-some? (subr running ((subr running (mentry) bool) (listof mentry acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (p es) (cond ((null? es) #f) ((p (car es)) #t) (else (m-some? p (cdr es)))))))

      (define-rec
        (m-where (subr running ((subr running (mentry) bool) (listof mentry acyclic)) (listof mentry acyclic))
          (lambda (p es) (cond ((null? es) nil) ((p (car es)) (cons (car es) (m-where p (cdr es)))) (else (m-where p (cdr es)))))))

      (define-rec
        (some-number? (subr running ((subr running (i64) bool) (listof i64 acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (p ns) (cond ((null? ns) #f) ((p (car ns)) #t) (else (some-number? p (cdr ns)))))))

      (define m-may-run? (subr running (mentry) bool)
        (lambda (e)
          "Whether `e` may take a slice now: unfinished, the results it names
           made, and no entry before it that it must wait for: in plain mode
           any; else, one that is not quiet, or any if `e` is not."
          (and (or (i64= (get (extract e state)) st-waiting) (i64= (get (extract e state)) st-running))
               (not (some-number? (lambda ((k i64))
                            (let ((found (m-numbered (get m-entries) k)))
                              (and (not (null? found)) (m-unfinished? (car found)))))
                          (extract e needs)))
               (not (m-some? (lambda ((d mentry))
                            (and (i64< (extract d num) (extract e num))
                                 (m-unfinished? d)
                                 (or (not (get m-live)) (not (extract e quiet)) (not (extract d quiet)))))
                          (get m-entries))))))

      (define parked-cleared! (subr running (i64) unit)
        (lambda (slot)
          "A task's registers dropped, so that the collector keeps nothing for it."
          (begin
            (roots-room! slot)
            (let ((r (get roots)) (at (parked-at slot)))
              (begin (flatarray-set-i64! r (i64+ at 2) 0) (flatarray-set-i64! r (i64+ at 3) w-nil)
                     (flatarray-set-i64! r (i64+ at 4) 0) (flatarray-set-i64! r (i64+ at 5) 0) (flatarray-set-i64! r (i64+ at 6) w-nil))))))

      (define m-noted! (subr running (string bool) unit)
        (lambda (text error)
          "The draft's run's outcome, for the front."
          (if (string=? text "") #u (set m-news (cons (draft-told (get m-spec-serial) text error) (get m-news))))))

      (define m-spec-dropped! (subr running () unit)
        (lambda ()
          "The draft's run forgotten: its task's registers, and the IR it was
           numbered into."
          (if (i64= (get m-spec-state) 0)
              #u
              (begin
                (if (i64= (get m-spec-state) 1) (parked-cleared! 0) #u)
                (let ((ms (get m-spec-marks)))
                  (if (i64= (size ms) 4)
                      (begin
                        (set node-count (car ms))
                        (set kid-count (car (cdr ms)))
                        (set armx-count (car (cdr (cdr ms))))
                        (set constant-count (car (cdr (cdr (cdr ms))))))
                      #u))
                (set m-spec-state 0)))))

      (define-rec
        (lowered! (subr running (i64 sexps (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (k forms tops)
            "Each form lowered and numbered, as the front's worker lowered it: an
             expression's value `%k`'s global."
            (if (null? forms)
                tops
                (let* ((form (car forms))
                       (expression (not (definition-form? form)))
                       (name (string-append "%" (i64->string k)))
                       (gs (onto (get repl-globals) (new-names (if expression (list name) (global-names (list form))) (get repl-globals)))))
                  (begin
                    (set repl-globals gs)
                    (globals-room! gs)
                    (let ((ns (number-tops! (lower-tops (list form) gs))))
                      (lowered! k (cdr forms) (onto tops (concat (map (lambda ((n i64)) (if (i64= n -1) nil (list n))) ns)))))))))))

      (define m-given! (subr running (i64 string string bool string string bool (listof i64 acyclic) i64) unit)
        (lambda (k text label timed typed defined quiet needs now)
          "An entry the front checked: lowered and numbered, and made a task.
           What the engine cannot number refuses it (C110)."
          (begin
            (m-spec-dropped!)
            (set repl-count k)
            (let* ((forms (read-all (string-chars text) (if (string=? label "") (string-append "<fx26:" (string-append (i64->string k) ">")) label) 1))
                   (tops (lowered! k forms nil)))
              (if (get engine-failed)
                  (set m-entries (cons (m-made k typed defined quiet needs st-refused nil (failure-taken!) timed now) (get m-entries)))
                  (set m-entries (cons (m-made k typed defined quiet needs st-waiting tops "" timed now) (get m-entries))))))))

      (define m-draft-run! (subr running (i64 string string) unit)
        (lambda (serial text type)
          "The draft's run begun, as the task in slot 0, its outcome a note sent
           back with `serial`."
          (begin
            (m-spec-dropped!)
            (set m-spec-serial serial)
            (set m-spec-type type)
            (set m-spec-marks (list (get node-count) (get kid-count) (get armx-count) (get constant-count)))
            ;; Ended until it starts: the tables given back even if numbering fails.
            (set m-spec-state 2)
            (let ((forms (read-all (string-chars text) "<draft>" 1)))
              (if (null? forms)
                  #u
                  (let ((ns (number-tops! (lower-tops (list (car forms)) (get repl-globals)))))
                    (cond ((get engine-failed) (m-noted! (string-append "running it fails: " (failure-taken!)) #t))
                          ((or (null? ns) (i64< (car ns) 0)) #u)
                          (else (begin (start-parked! 0 (car ns)) (set m-spec-steps 0) (set m-spec-state 1))))))))))

      (define m-interrupted! (subr running (mentry i64) unit)
        (lambda (e now)
          (begin
            (m-ended! e st-interrupted now)
            (parked-cleared! (extract e num)))))

      (define m-asked! (subr (maxeff running (io terminal)) (asked i64) unit)
        (lambda (r now)
          "A request from the front."
          (tagcase r
            (entry-asked (k text label timed typed defined quiet needs) (m-given! k text label timed typed defined quiet needs now))
            (draft-asked (serial text type) (m-draft-run! serial text type))
            (draft-unasked () (m-spec-dropped!))
            (cancel-asked (k)
              (let ((found (m-numbered (get m-entries) k)))
                (if (and (not (null? found)) (m-unfinished? (car found))) (m-interrupted! (car found) now) #u)))
            (limit-asked (n) (set m-step-limit n))
            (round-ended (clock reply) #u)
            (front-ended () (set m-over #t))
            (front-failed (m)
              (begin
                (terminal-restore)
                (write-err (string-append "kayak-fx26: the REPL's front failed: " (string-append m "\n")))
                (set m-over #t))))))

      "Running, by slices."

      (define slice-timed! (subr running () unit)
        (lambda ()
          "A slice's deadline, if the session is live (a scripted one's slices
           are steps alone, so that it replays the same)."
          (if (i64>= (get m-slice-ns) 0) (set deadline (i64+ (clock) (get m-slice-ns))) #u)))

      (define m-run-failed! (subr running (i64 string i64) unit)
        (lambda (k message now)
          "Entry `k`'s run failed, the engine said (C110); or the draft's."
          (begin
            (set fuel -1)
            (set deadline -1)
            (set capturing #f)
            (let ((found (m-numbered (get m-entries) k)))
              (cond ((i64= k 0)
                     (begin
                       (set m-spec-state 2)
                       (parked-cleared! 0)
                       (m-noted! (string-append "running it fails: " message) #t)))
                    ((null? found) #u)
                    (else
                     (let ((e (car found)))
                       (begin
                         (taken-output! e)
                         (m-ended! e st-failed now)
                         (set (extract e shown) (string-append "! evaluation failed: " message))
                         (parked-cleared! k)))))))))

      (define draft-runnable? (subr running () bool)
        (lambda ()
          "Whether the draft's run may take a slice: begun, not ended, and no
           entry unfinished that does more than read and allocate."
          (and (i64= (get m-spec-state) 1)
               (not (m-some? (lambda ((d mentry)) (and (m-unfinished? d) (not (extract d quiet)))) (get m-entries))))))

      (define draft-slice! (subr running (i64) unit)
        (lambda (now)
          "A slice of the draft's run."
          (begin
            (set m-last-run 0)
            (set task-slot 0)
            (set fuel slice-steps)
            (slice-timed!)
            (let ((w (resume 0)))
              (begin
                (set m-spec-steps (i64+ (get m-spec-steps) (i64- slice-steps (get fuel))))
                (set fuel -1)
                (set deadline -1)
                (cond ((get engine-failed) (m-run-failed! 0 (failure-taken!) now))
                      ((not (i64= w w-paused))
                       (begin
                         (set m-spec-state 2)
                         (parked-cleared! 0)
                         (m-noted! (string-append "= " (string-append (show-word w) (get m-spec-type))) #f)))
                      ((i64> (get m-spec-steps) spec-limit)
                       (begin
                         (set m-spec-state 2)
                         (parked-cleared! 0)
                         (m-noted! (string-append "…" (string-append (get m-spec-type) (string-append "  (not run to its end early: " (string-append (i64->string spec-limit) " steps; Enter runs it)")))) #f)))
                      (else #u)))))))

      (define start-top! (subr running (mentry) unit)
        (lambda (e)
          (let ((ts (get (extract e tops))))
            (if (null? ts) #u (start-parked! (extract e num) (if (i64< (car ts) 0) (i64- (i64- 0 (car ts)) 2) (car ts)))))))

      (define-rec
        (global-index (subr running (string strings i64) i64)
          (lambda (n gs i) (cond ((null? gs) -1) ((string=? (car gs) n) i) (else (global-index n (cdr gs) (i64+ i 1)))))))

      (define top-ended! (subr running (mentry i64 i64) unit)
        (lambda (e w now)
          "A top ended (its number not negative if an expression, whose value
           is then `%k`'s): the next begun, or the entry done."
          (let* ((ts (get (extract e tops)))
                 (rest (if (null? ts) nil (cdr ts)))
                 (i (global-index (string-append "%" (i64->string (extract e num))) (get repl-globals) 0)))
            (begin
              (if (and (i64>= i 0) (not (null? ts)) (i64>= (car ts) 0)) (flatarray-set-i64! (get globals) i w) #u)
              (set (extract e tops) rest)
              (if (null? rest)
                  (begin
                    (m-ended! e st-done now)
                    (set (extract e shown)
                         (let ((value (if (i64< i 0) "" (string-append (show-word (flatarray-ref-i64 (get globals) i)) (extract e typed)))))
                           (cond ((string=? value "") (extract e defined))
                                 ((string=? (extract e defined) "") value)
                                 (else (string-append (extract e defined) (string-append "\n" value))))))
                    (parked-cleared! (extract e num)))
                  (start-top! e))))))

      (define taken-output! (subr running (mentry) unit)
        (lambda (e)
          (begin
            (set (extract e out) (string-append (get (extract e out)) (rev->string (get captured))))
            (set captured nil))))

      (define next-task (subr running () i64)
        (lambda ()
          "The entry to run a slice of, by turns, or -1; 0, the draft's run."
          (let* ((ready (m-where m-may-run? (m-oldest-first (get m-entries) nil)))
                 (last (get m-last-run))
                 (after (m-where (lambda ((e mentry)) (i64> (extract e num) last)) ready)))
            (cond ((not (null? after)) (extract (car after) num))
                  ((draft-runnable?) 0)
                  ((not (null? ready)) (extract (car ready) num))
                  (else -1)))))

      (define slice! (subr running (i64 i64) unit)
        (lambda (k now)
          "A slice of entry `k`: its tops run on from where they paused; or of
           the draft's run, `k` 0."
          (let ((found (m-numbered (get m-entries) k)))
            (cond ((i64= k 0) (draft-slice! now))
                  ((null? found) #u)
                  (else
                   (let ((e (car found)))
                     (begin
                       (set m-last-run k)
                       (if (i64= (get (extract e state)) st-waiting)
                           (begin (set (extract e state) st-running) (start-top! e))
                           #u)
                       (set task-slot k)
                       (set fuel slice-steps)
                       (slice-timed!)
                       (set capturing #t)
                       (let ((w (if (null? (get (extract e tops))) w-unit (resume k))))
                         (begin
                           (set (extract e steps) (i64+ (get (extract e steps)) (i64- slice-steps (get fuel))))
                           (set fuel -1)
                           (set deadline -1)
                           (set capturing #f)
                           (taken-output! e)
                           (cond ((get engine-failed) (m-run-failed! k (failure-traced! "!   ") now))
                                 ((not (i64= w w-paused)) (top-ended! e w now))
                                 ((and (i64>= (get m-step-limit) 0) (i64> (get (extract e steps)) (get m-step-limit)))
                                  (begin
                                    (m-ended! e st-failed now)
                                    (set (extract e shown) (string-append "! the step limit, " (string-append (i64->string (get m-step-limit)) ", reached (,step-limit)")))
                                    (parked-cleared! k)))
                                 (else #u)))))))))))

      "What the front is told."

      (define entry-key (subr running (mentry) string)
        (lambda (e)
          "What the front is told of an entry, apart from its output and steps,
           as a text, to know when it changed (C103)."
          (string-append (i64->string (get (extract e state)))
                         (string-append "|" (string-append (i64->string (get (extract e ended))) (string-append "|" (get (extract e shown))))))))

      (define-rec
        (entries-news (subr running ((listof mentry acyclic)) (listof told acyclic))
          (lambda (es)
            "Each entry as it is now, its output since taken, for the front."
            (if (null? es)
                nil
                (let* ((e (car es)) (out (get (extract e out))))
                  (begin
                    (set (extract e out) "")
                    (set (extract e drawn) (entry-key e))
                    (cons (entry-told (extract e num) (get (extract e state)) (get (extract e shown)) out
                                      (get (extract e began)) (get (extract e ended)) (get (extract e steps))
                                      (i64- (if (i64< (get (extract e gcs-after)) 0) (get collections) (get (extract e gcs-after))) (extract e gcs)))
                          (entries-news (cdr es)))))))))

      (define news-taken! (subr running () (listof told acyclic))
        (lambda ()
          "The news not yet sent, the oldest first: each entry whose state or
           line changed, or that wrote; then the draft's run's outcome."
          (let ((es (m-where (lambda ((e mentry))
                               (or (not (string=? (get (extract e out)) ""))
                                   (not (string=? (entry-key e) (get (extract e drawn))))))
                             (m-oldest-first (get m-entries) nil)))
                (drafts (get m-news)))
            (begin
              (set m-news nil)
              (onto (entries-news es) (reversed-onto drafts nil))))))

      "The machine's loops: asking the relay for the front's requests, by an
       I-cell, waiting for one or not."


      (define asked-of (subr machining ((addr relayed @m) bool) (listof asked acyclic))
        (lambda (relay waiting)
          (let ((c (the (icell (listof asked acyclic) @m) (make-icell))))
            (begin (send relay (taken c waiting)) (icell-get c)))))

      (define now-ms (subr (io clock) () i64) (lambda () (i64-quotient (clock) 1000000)))

      (define-rec
        (each-asked! (subr machining ((listof asked acyclic) i64) unit)
          (lambda (rs now) (if (null? rs) #u (begin (m-asked! (car rs) now) (each-asked! (cdr rs) now))))))

      (define-rec
        (each-told! (subr machining ((addr told @f) (listof told acyclic)) unit)
          (lambda (front ns) (if (null? ns) #u (begin (send front (car ns)) (each-told! front (cdr ns)))))))

      (define-rec
        (live-slices! (subr machining ((addr relayed @m) i64) unit)
          (lambda (relay began)
            "Slices, the entries by turns, for a sixtieth of a second at most,
             or until a request comes, which is taken then."
            (let ((k (next-task)) (now (now-ms)))
              (if (or (i64< k 0) (i64>= (i64- now began) 16))
                  #u
                  (begin
                    (slice! k now)
                    (let ((rs (asked-of relay #f)))
                      (if (null? rs) (live-slices! relay began) (each-asked! rs (now-ms))))))))))

      (define-rec
        (machine-live! (subr machining ((addr relayed @m) (addr told @f)) unit)
          (lambda (relay front)
            "The machine of a live or plain session (C103's, in FX-26): requests
             taken, waited for when nothing may run; slices; the news sent."
            (begin
              (each-asked! (asked-of relay (i64< (next-task) 0)) (now-ms))
              (if (get m-over)
                  #u
                  (begin
                    (live-slices! relay (now-ms))
                    (each-told! front (news-taken!))
                    (machine-live! relay front)))))))

      (define-rec
        (scripted-slices! (subr machining (i64 i64) i64)
          (lambda (clock n)
            "At most `n` slices, a millisecond each on the virtual clock: the
             clock after them. The clock is read, and moves, at each look for a
             task, the last too, which finds none or is past `n`, as C103's did."
            (let ((k (next-task)) (t (i64+ clock 1)))
              (if (or (i64< k 0) (i64<= n 0))
                  t
                  (begin (slice! k t) (scripted-slices! t (i64- n 1))))))))

      (define-rec
        (round-of (subr kfx ((listof asked acyclic)) (listof asked acyclic))
          (lambda (rs)
            "The first round's end among `rs`, if any."
            (cond ((null? rs) nil)
                  ((tagcase (car rs) (round-ended (c r) #t) (else o #f)) (list (car rs)))
                  (else (round-of (cdr rs))))))
        (before-round (subr kfx ((listof asked acyclic)) (listof asked acyclic))
          (lambda (rs)
            (cond ((null? rs) nil)
                  ((tagcase (car rs) (round-ended (c r) #t) (else o #f)) nil)
                  (else (cons (car rs) (before-round (cdr rs)))))))
        (after-round (subr kfx ((listof asked acyclic)) (listof asked acyclic))
          (lambda (rs)
            (cond ((null? rs) nil)
                  ((tagcase (car rs) (round-ended (c r) #t) (else o #f)) (cdr rs))
                  (else (after-round (cdr rs)))))))

      (define-rec
        (ends? (subr kfx ((listof asked acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (rs)
            (cond ((null? rs) #f)
                  ((tagcase (car rs) (front-ended () #t) (front-failed (m) #t) (else o #f)) #t)
                  (else (ends? (cdr rs)))))))

      (define-rec
        (machine-scripted! (subr machining ((addr relayed @m) (listof asked acyclic)) unit)
          (lambda (relay pending)
            "The machine of a scripted session, in step with the front (C103):
             a round's requests taken at its clock, then 16 slices at most; what
             they ran put where the front waits. Requests wait for their round's
             end, which says the clock."
            (let ((round (round-of pending)))
              (cond ((get m-over) #u)
                    ((not (null? round))
                     (tagcase (car round)
                       (round-ended (clock reply)
                         (begin
                           (each-asked! (before-round pending) clock)
                           (let ((after (scripted-slices! clock 16)))
                             (begin
                               (icell-put! reply (ran (news-taken!) after (i64< (next-task) 0)))
                               (machine-scripted! relay (after-round pending))))))
                       (else o #u)))
                    ((ends? pending) (each-asked! pending 0))
                    (else (machine-scripted! relay (onto pending (asked-of relay #t)))))))))

      "The relay (C111): the machine's mailbox. What the front asks is kept,
       the oldest first, until the machine takes it, at once or once there is
       some."
      (define relay-made (subr (maxeff (alloc @m) (init @m) nondet spin (read @globals)) () (addr relayed @m))
        (lambda ()
          (spawn (box relayed p)
            (letrec ((relaying (subr (maxeff (receive p) (init @m) nondet spin (read @globals)) ((listof asked acyclic) (listof (icell (listof asked acyclic) @m) acyclic)) unit)
                       (lambda (kept waiting)
                         (tagcase (receive box)
                           (from-front (r)
                             (if (null? waiting)
                                 (relaying (cons r kept) waiting)
                                 (begin (icell-put! (car waiting) (reversed-onto (cons r kept) nil)) (relaying nil nil))))
                           (taken (c wait)
                             (if (and wait (null? kept))
                                 (relaying kept (list c))
                                 (begin (icell-put! c (reversed-onto kept nil)) (relaying nil nil))))))))
              (relaying nil nil)))))


      "The front (C111): a process, its state in its place, `r`, which its
       procedures are polymorphic in, since FX-26 lets a process write its
       place alone. An entry as the front keeps it: its number, text, what
       is written after its value, its definitions' lines, whether quiet, the
       results it names; its state, line, output not yet written, when it
       began and ended, the row its line is on (-1 if not yet written), the
       line as last drawn, whether timed, its steps and collections as the
       machine told them."
      (define-type (fentry (r region))
        (productof (num i64) (text string) (typed string) (defined string) (quiet bool) (needs (listof i64 acyclic))
                   (state (ref i64 r)) (shown (ref string r)) (out (ref string r)) (began (ref i64 r)) (ended (ref i64 r))
                   (row (ref i64 r)) (drawn (ref string r)) (timed bool) (steps (ref i64 r)) (collected (ref i64 r))))

      "The front's state: the draft's speculation (C96, C97), as C103's
       session had it; the screen, the draft and its editing, the history,
       the commands; the requests not yet sent; the checker's environment,
       the globals' names and the entries' count, as the machine will have
       them; whether the input has ended; and the relay's address."
      (define-type (fstate (r region))
        (productof (note (ref string r)) (note-error (ref bool r)) (speculated (ref bool r)) (spec-kept (ref i64 r))
                   (spec-open (ref (listof i64 acyclic) r)) (spec-finished (ref bool r)) (spec-type (ref string r))
                   (spec-state (ref i64 r)) (spec-key (ref string r)) (spec-waits (ref bool r)) (spec-serial (ref i64 r))
                   (spec-text (ref string r)) (spec-phase (ref i64 r)) (hole-texts (ref strings r)) (trying-holes (ref bool r))
                   (hole-at (ref i64 r)) (hole-op (ref string r)) (hole-place (ref i64 r)) (around (ref string r))
                   (around-at (ref i64 r)) (under-from (ref i64 r)) (under-to (ref i64 r))
                   (live (ref bool r)) (screen-rows (ref i64 r)) (screen-cols (ref i64 r))
                   (entries (ref (listof (fentry r) acyclic) r)) (draft (ref string r)) (rows (ref i64 r))
                   (draft-rows (ref i64 r)) (draft-dirty (ref bool r)) (leaving (ref bool r)) (escape (ref i64 r))
                   (written (ref chars r)) (cursor (ref i64 r)) (cursor-row (ref i64 r)) (escape-param (ref i64 r))
                   (history (ref strings r)) (history-at (ref i64 r)) (stash (ref string r)) (history-path (ref string r))
                   (step-limit (ref i64 r)) (commands (ref i64 r)) (quitting (ref bool r))
                   (requests (ref (listof asked acyclic) r)) (cv (ref cv r)) (globals (ref strings r)) (count (ref i64 r))
                   (input-ended (ref bool r)) (relay (addr relayed @m))))


      "Entries, by number and state."

      (define* f-unfinished? (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r)) ((fentry r)) bool))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (e)
            (let ((s (get (extract e state))))
              (or (i64= s st-checking) (i64= s st-waiting) (i64= s st-running))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-numbered (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) spin) ((listof (fentry r) acyclic) i64) (listof (fentry r) acyclic)))
          (lambda (es k)
            (cond ((null? es) nil)
                  ((i64= (extract (car es) num) k) (list (car es)))
                  (else (f-numbered (cdr es) k))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-oldest-first (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff spin (read @globals)) ((listof (fentry r) acyclic) (listof (fentry r) acyclic)) (listof (fentry r) acyclic)))
          (lambda (es acc) (if (null? es) acc (f-oldest-first (cdr es) (cons (car es) acc))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-unfinished (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) spin) ((listof (fentry r) acyclic)) (listof (fentry r) acyclic)))
          (lambda (es)
            (cond ((null? es) nil)
                  ((f-unfinished? (car es)) (cons (car es) (f-unfinished (cdr es))))
                  (else (f-unfinished (cdr es)))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-unwritten? (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) spin) ((listof (fentry r) acyclic)) bool))
          (lambda (es) (cond ((null? es) #f) ((i64< (get (extract (car es) row)) 0) #t) (else (f-unwritten? (cdr es)))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-unfinished-of (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) spin) ((listof (fentry r) acyclic) (listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic)))
          (lambda (es ks)
            "The entries numbered `ks` that have not ended."
            (cond ((null? ks) nil)
                  ((let ((found (f-numbered es (car ks)))) (and (not (null? found)) (f-unfinished? (car found))))
                   (cons (car ks) (f-unfinished-of es (cdr ks))))
                  (else (f-unfinished-of es (cdr ks)))))))

      (define* f-made (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) (i64 string string string bool (listof i64 acyclic) i64 string bool i64) (fentry r)))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (k text typed defined quiet needs state shown timed now)
            (product (num k) (text text) (typed typed) (defined defined) (quiet quiet) (needs needs)
                     (state (new state)) (shown (new shown)) (out (new ""))
                     (began (new now)) (ended (new (if (i64= state st-done) now -1))) (row (new -1)) (drawn (new ""))
                     (timed timed) (steps (new 0)) (collected (new 0))))))

      (define* f-say! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f s) (set (extract f written) (put s (get (extract f written)))))))

      (define* f-up! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals)) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f n) (if (i64> n 0) (f-say! f (string-append "\x1b;[" (string-append (i64->string n) "A"))) #u))))

      (define* f-down! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals)) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f n) (if (i64> n 0) (f-say! f (string-append "\x1b;[" (string-append (i64->string n) "B"))) #u))))

      (define* f-asked! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) asked) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f q) (set (extract f requests) (cons q (get (extract f requests)))))))

      (define* f-requests-sent! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            "The requests not yet sent, the oldest first, to the relay."
            (let ((qs (reversed-onto (get (extract f requests)) nil)))
              (begin
                (set (extract f requests) nil)
                (letrec ((each (subr (maxeff fronting) ((addr relayed @m) (listof asked acyclic)) unit)
                           (lambda (to qs) (if (null? qs) #u (begin (send to (from-front (car qs))) (each to (cdr qs)))))))
                  (each (extract f relay) qs)))))))

      "What an entry's line says."

      (define* f-entry-line (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) (fentry r) i64) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f e now)
            (let* ((s (get (extract e state)))
                   (live (get (extract f live)))
                   (head (if (and live (i64> (extract e num) 0)) (string-append "[" (string-append (i64->string (extract e num)) "] ")) ""))
                   (took (i64- (if (i64>= (get (extract e ended)) 0) (get (extract e ended)) now) (get (extract e began))))
                   (time (cond ((extract e timed)
                                (string-append "  (" (string-append (seconds took)
                                  (string-append ", " (string-append (i64->string (get (extract e steps)))
                                    (string-append " steps, " (string-append (i64->string (get (extract e collected))) " collections)")))))))
                               ((and live (i64>= took 100)) (string-append "  (" (string-append (seconds took) ")")))
                               (else ""))))
              (cond ((i64= s st-checking) (string-append head "…"))
                    ((i64= s st-waiting) (string-append head (string-append (spinner now) " waiting")))
                    ((i64= s st-running) (string-append head (string-append (spinner now) (string-append " running " (seconds took)))))
                    ((i64= s st-done) (string-append head (string-append (get (extract e shown)) time)))
                    ((i64= s st-interrupted) (string-append head (string-append "interrupted" time)))
                    (else (string-append head (get (extract e shown)))))))))

      "The note under the draft."

      (define* f-noted! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r)) ((fstate r) string bool) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f text error)
            (begin (set (extract f note) text) (set (extract f note-error) error) (set (extract f draft-dirty) #t)))))

      (define* f-note-shown (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r)) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            "The note as drawn: its first line, cut to the screen's width."
            (let* ((line (first-line (get (extract f note))))
                   (width (i64- (get (extract f screen-cols)) 1))
                   (cut-short (or (i64> (string-length-i64 line) width) (has-char-in? (get (extract f note)) #\newline))))
              (if cut-short (string-append (cut line 0 (i64- width 1)) "…") line)))))

      "The screen."

      (define* f-draw-draft! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f d)
            "The draft drawn from the start of its first row, the rows below
             cleared; its note, if any, on the row after it."
            (let ((cs (string-chars d)) (shown (f-note-shown f)) (cols (get (extract f screen-cols))))
              (begin
                (f-say! f "\r\x1b;[J")
                (f-say! f "fx26> ")
                (set (extract f written) (prompted cs 0 (get (extract f under-from)) (get (extract f under-to)) (get (extract f written))))
                (if (string=? shown "")
                    #u
                    (begin (f-say! f "\r\n") (f-say! f (if (get (extract f note-error)) "\x1b;[31m" "\x1b;[2m")) (f-say! f shown) (f-say! f "\x1b;[0m")))
                (set (extract f draft-rows) (i64+ (wrapped-rows cs 6 cols 1) (if (string=? shown "") 0 1)))
                (set (extract f draft-dirty) #f)
                (let* ((before (string-chars (substring d 0 (i64->int (get (extract f cursor))))))
                       (row (i64- (wrapped-rows before 6 cols 1) 1))
                       (col (column-after before 6 cols)))
                  (begin
                    (if (and (i64= (get (extract f cursor)) (string-length-i64 d)) (string=? shown ""))
                        #u
                        (begin
                          (f-up! f (i64- (i64- (get (extract f draft-rows)) 1) row))
                          (f-say! f "\r")
                          (if (i64> col 0) (f-say! f (string-append "\x1b;[" (string-append (i64->string col) "C"))) #u)))
                    (set (extract f cursor-row) row))))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-printed-lines! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) strings) unit))
          (lambda (f ls)
            "Rows added to the transcript, above the draft: each line."
            (if (null? ls)
                #u
                (let ((live (get (extract f live))))
                  (begin
                    (f-say! f (if live "\x1b;[2K" ""))
                    (f-say! f (car ls))
                    (f-say! f (if live "\r\n" "\n"))
                    (set (extract f rows) (i64+ (get (extract f rows)) (wrapped-rows (string-chars (car ls)) 0 (get (extract f screen-cols)) 1)))
                    (f-printed-lines! f (cdr ls))))))))

      (define* f-printed! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f text) (f-printed-lines! f (lines-of (string-chars text) nil nil)))))

      (define-rec
        (f-output-printed! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64 strings) unit))
          (lambda (f k ls)
            (if (null? ls)
                #u
                (begin
                  (f-printed! f (string-append "[" (string-append (i64->string k) (string-append "]│ " (car ls)))))
                  (f-output-printed! f k (cdr ls)))))))

      (define* f-entry-drawn! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) (fentry r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f e now)
            "An entry's output, as rows above the draft, and its line: written
             new if not yet, rewritten where it is if changed and on the screen,
             or written new if it ended off the screen. The cursor is left at the
             draft's first row."
            (let ((out (get (extract e out))))
              (begin
                (if (string=? out "")
                    #u
                    (begin
                      (set (extract e out) "")
                      (f-output-printed! f (extract e num) (lines-of (string-chars out) nil nil))))
                (let* ((line (f-entry-line f e now))
                       (row (get (extract e row)))
                       (up (i64- (get (extract f rows)) row)))
                  (cond ((string=? line (get (extract e drawn))) #u)
                        ((i64< row 0)
                         (begin (set (extract e row) (get (extract f rows))) (set (extract e drawn) line) (f-printed! f line)))
                        ((and (i64< up (i64- (get (extract f screen-rows)) (get (extract f draft-rows)))) (not (has-char-in? line #\newline)))
                         (begin
                           (set (extract e drawn) line)
                           (f-up! f up)
                           (f-say! f "\r\x1b;[2K")
                           (f-say! f line)
                           (f-down! f up)
                           (f-say! f "\r")))
                        ((f-unfinished? e) #u)
                        (else (begin (set (extract e row) (get (extract f rows))) (set (extract e drawn) line) (f-printed! f line))))))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-each-drawn! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) (listof (fentry r) acyclic) i64) unit))
          (lambda (f es now) (if (null? es) #u (begin (f-entry-drawn! f (car es) now) (f-each-drawn! f (cdr es) now))))))

      (define* f-live-screen! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            (let ((es (f-oldest-first (get (extract f entries)) nil))
                  (before (rev->string (get (extract f written)))))
              (begin
                (set (extract f written) nil)
                ;; To the draft's first row.
                (f-up! f (get (extract f cursor-row)))
                (f-say! f "\r")
                (let ((moved (rev->string (get (extract f written)))))
                  (begin
                    (set (extract f written) nil)
                    (f-each-drawn! f es now)
                    (let ((changes (rev->string (get (extract f written)))))
                      (begin
                        (set (extract f written) (put before nil))
                        (if (and (string=? changes "") (not (get (extract f draft-dirty))))
                            #u
                            (begin
                              (f-say! f moved)
                              (f-say! f changes)
                              (f-draw-draft! f (get (extract f draft))))))))))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-each-plain! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) (listof (fentry r) acyclic) i64) unit))
          (lambda (f es now)
            (if (null? es)
                #u
                (let ((e (car es)))
                  (begin
                    (if (string=? (get (extract e out)) "") #u (begin (f-say! f (get (extract e out))) (set (extract e out) "")))
                    (if (and (not (f-unfinished? e)) (i64< (get (extract e row)) 0))
                        (let ((line (f-entry-line f e now)))
                          (begin (set (extract e row) 0) (if (string=? line "") #u (f-say! f (string-append line "\n")))))
                        #u)
                    (f-each-plain! f (cdr es) now)))))))

      (define* f-screen! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            "What to write: in plain mode, each entry's output, and its line when
             it ends, in order; live, the lines that changed, rewritten in place
             if on the screen, new rows above the draft, and the draft."
            (begin
              (if (get (extract f live)) (f-live-screen! f now) (f-each-plain! f (f-oldest-first (get (extract f entries)) nil) now))
              (let ((s (rev->string (get (extract f written))))) (begin (set (extract f written) nil) s))))))

      "Editing: the draft and the cursor in it, a character's index."

      (define* f-draft-set! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f d at)
            (begin
              (if (string=? d (get (extract f draft))) #u (set (extract f speculated) #f))
              (set (extract f draft) d) (set (extract f cursor) (clamped at (string-length-i64 d))) (set (extract f draft-dirty) #t)))))

      (define* f-inserted! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f text)
            (let ((d (get (extract f draft))) (at (get (extract f cursor))))
              (f-draft-set! f (string-append (cut d 0 at) (string-append text (cut d at (string-length-i64 d))))
                            (i64+ at (string-length-i64 text)))))))

      (define* f-deleted! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64 i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f from to)
            (let* ((d (get (extract f draft))) (n (string-length-i64 d)) (a (clamped from n)) (b (clamped to n)))
              (if (i64>= a b) #u (f-draft-set! f (string-append (cut d 0 a) (cut d b n)) a))))))

      (define* f-moved! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f at) (begin (set (extract f cursor) (clamped at (string-length-i64 (get (extract f draft))))) (set (extract f draft-dirty) #t)))))

      (define* f-ended! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r)) ((fstate r) (fentry r) i64 i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f e state now)
            "An entry ended, in `state`: when; a draft that waited for one tried
             again."
            (begin
              (set (extract e state) state)
              (set (extract e ended) now)
              (if (get (extract f spec-waits)) (begin (set (extract f speculated) #f) (set (extract f spec-key) "")) #u)))))

      (define* f-speculation-dropped! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            "The draft's speculation forgotten: its run, on the machine, and its
             note."
            (begin
              (if (i64= (get (extract f spec-state)) 1) (f-asked! f (draft-unasked)) #u)
              (set (extract f spec-state) 0)
              (set (extract f speculated) #f)
              (set (extract f spec-key) "")
              (set (extract f spec-waits) #f)
              (set (extract f spec-phase) 4)
              (set (extract f around) "")
              (set (extract f around-at) -1)
              (set (extract f under-from) 0)
              (set (extract f under-to) 0)
              (if (string=? (get (extract f note)) "") #u (f-noted! f "" #f))))))

      (define* f-finish-draft! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            "The draft, whole, left on the screen as it was drawn: the rows below
             it the transcript's. The entries' lines not yet written are written
             first, so that an entry given in the same keys as the one before it
             (pasted) comes after that one's line."
            (if (get (extract f live))
                (begin
                  (if (f-unwritten? (get (extract f entries))) (f-live-screen! f now) #u)
                  (f-up! f (get (extract f cursor-row)))
                  (set (extract f note) "")
                  (set (extract f under-from) 0)
                  (set (extract f under-to) 0)
                  (set (extract f cursor) (string-length-i64 (get (extract f draft))))
                  (f-draw-draft! f (get (extract f draft)))
                  (f-say! f "\r\n")
                  (set (extract f rows) (i64+ (get (extract f rows)) (get (extract f draft-rows))))
                  (set (extract f draft-rows) 1)
                  (set (extract f cursor-row) 0)
                  (set (extract f draft-dirty) #t))
                #u))))

      "History: a file of entries, each a line, its newlines and backslashes
       escaped; the last 500 kept."

      (define* f-history-written! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (alloc r) (io fs-write) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            (if (string=? (get (extract f history-path)) "")
                #u
                (tagcase (write-file (get (extract f history-path)) (the (bytevectorof r) (string->utf8 (rev->string (history-text (get (extract f history)) 500 nil)))))
                  (done u #u)
                  (failed e #u))))))

      (define* f-history-read! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (io fs-read) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            (if (string=? (get (extract f history-path)) "")
                #u
                (tagcase (the (sumof (data (bytevectorof r)) (failed io-error)) (read-file (get (extract f history-path))))
                  (data b (tagcase (utf8->string b)
                            (text t (set (extract f history)
                                         (oldest-first-strings (map (lambda ((l string)) (rev->string (unescaped (string-chars l) nil)))
                                                                    (lines-of (string-chars t) nil nil))
                                                               nil)))
                            (bad k #u)))
                  (failed e #u))))))

      (define* f-history-moved! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f by)
            "Up (`by` 1) to an older entry's text, or down; past the newest, the
             draft that was put aside."
            (let ((to (i64+ (get (extract f history-at)) by)) (n (size (get (extract f history)))))
              (cond ((i64>= to n) #u)
                    ((i64< to 0)
                     (if (i64< (get (extract f history-at)) 0)
                         #u
                         (begin (set (extract f history-at) -1) (f-draft-set! f (get (extract f stash)) (string-length-i64 (get (extract f stash)))))))
                    (else
                     (begin
                       (if (i64< (get (extract f history-at)) 0) (set (extract f stash) (get (extract f draft))) #u)
                       (set (extract f history-at) to)
                       (let ((t (nth-string (get (extract f history)) to))) (f-draft-set! f t (string-length-i64 t))))))))))

      (define* f-escaped! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64 i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f c now)
            "An escape sequence's final key: up and down move between the draft's
             lines, or through the history at its first or last; left, right,
             Home, End, Delete."
            (let* ((d (get (extract f draft))) (at (get (extract f cursor))) (start (line-start d at)) (param (get (extract f escape-param))))
              (cond ((i64= c 65) (if (i64= start 0) (f-history-moved! f 1) (f-moved! f (column-on d (line-start d (i64- start 1)) (i64- at start)))))
                    ((i64= c 66)
                     (let ((end (line-end d at)))
                       (if (i64>= end (string-length-i64 d)) (f-history-moved! f -1) (f-moved! f (column-on d (i64+ end 1) (i64- at start))))))
                    ((i64= c 67) (f-moved! f (i64+ at 1)))
                    ((i64= c 68) (f-moved! f (i64- at 1)))
                    ((i64= c 72) (f-moved! f start))
                    ((i64= c 70) (f-moved! f (line-end d at)))
                    ((and (i64= c 126) (i64= param 3)) (f-deleted! f at (i64+ at 1)))
                    ((and (i64= c 126) (i64= param 1)) (f-moved! f start))
                    ((and (i64= c 126) (i64= param 4)) (f-moved! f (line-end d at)))
                    (else #u))))))

      "Commands, and entries."

      (define* f-said! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f line now)
            "A command's line, as an entry's that is done."
            (begin
              (set (extract f commands) (i64+ (get (extract f commands)) 1))
              (set (extract f entries) (cons (f-made (i64- 0 (get (extract f commands))) "" "" "" #t nil st-done line #f now) (get (extract f entries))))))))

      (define* f-known-names (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r)) strings))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            (concat (map (lambda ((b bind)) (tagcase b (bind (n sc w) (if (or (has-prefix? n "%") (has-char-in? n #\space)) nil (list n)))))
                         (cv-binds (get (extract f cv))))))))

      (define* f-completed! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            "Tab: the name before the cursor completed as far as the names it
             begins agree; if that adds nothing and there are several, they are
             said."
            (let* ((d (get (extract f draft))) (at (get (extract f cursor))) (from (name-start d at)) (p (cut d from at))
                   (found (sorted-strings (deduped-names (concat (map (lambda ((n string)) (if (has-prefix? n p) (list n) nil)) (f-known-names f))) nil))))
              (cond ((or (string=? p "") (null? found)) #u)
                    (else
                     (let ((common (common-prefix (car found) (cdr found))))
                       (cond ((i64> (string-length-i64 common) (string-length-i64 p)) (f-inserted! f (cut common (string-length-i64 p) (string-length-i64 common))))
                             ((null? (cdr found)) #u)
                             (else (f-said! f (words-of-at-most found 12) now))))))))))

      (define* f-refused! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r)) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f message now)
            "The entry being checked refused (its worker failed)."
            (let ((es (get (extract f entries))))
              (if (or (null? es) (not (i64= (get (extract (car es) state)) st-checking)))
                  #u
                  (begin
                    (set (extract (car es) state) st-refused)
                    (set (extract (car es) shown) message)
                    (set (extract (car es) ended) now)))))))

      (define* f-submit! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string string bool i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f text label timed now)
            "An entry of `text`, its forms read as from `label` (`<fx26:k>`, or a
             file `,load` reads): checked by a worker, after the entries before
             it; given the machine, which lowers and runs it, if accepted."
            (let* ((k (i64+ (get (extract f count)) 1)))
              (begin
                (set (extract f count) k)
                (f-speculation-dropped! f)
                (set (extract f entries) (cons (f-made k text "" "" #t nil st-checking "" timed now) (get (extract f entries))))
                (tagcase (worked (check-entry (get (extract f cv)) (get (extract f globals)) k text label))
                  (entry-done (v gs typed defined quiet needs)
                    (begin
                      (set (extract f cv) v)
                      (set (extract f globals) gs)
                      (set (extract f entries) (cons (f-made k text typed defined quiet needs st-waiting "" timed now) (cdr (get (extract f entries)))))
                      (f-asked! f (entry-asked k text label timed typed defined quiet needs))))
                  (refused-done (m) (f-refused! f m now))
                  (else other #u)))))))

      (define* f-given! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f d now)
            "The draft left on the screen, kept in the history, and emptied."
            (begin
              (f-finish-draft! f now)
              (set (extract f history) (cons (trimmed-end d) (get (extract f history))))
              (f-history-written! f)
              (set (extract f history-at) -1)
              (set (extract f stash) "")
              (f-draft-set! f "" 0)))))

      (define* f-typed-only! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f text now)
            "`,type E`: E checked by a worker, its type and effect said, not run.
             A refusal finds the line, as an entry's (`f-refused!`)."
            (begin
              (set (extract f commands) (i64+ (get (extract f commands)) 1))
              (set (extract f entries) (cons (f-made (i64- 0 (get (extract f commands))) text "" "" #t nil st-checking "" #f now) (get (extract f entries))))
              (tagcase (worked (type-of (get (extract f cv)) text))
                (shown-done (shown)
                  (let ((e (car (get (extract f entries)))))
                    (begin
                      (set (extract e shown) (string-append text shown))
                      (set (extract e state) st-done)
                      (set (extract e ended) now))))
                (refused-done (m) (f-refused! f m now))
                (else other #u))))))

      (define* f-described (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f n)
            "`,help NAME`: NAME's type, as the checker has it."
            (let ((found (find-bind n (cv-binds (get (extract f cv))))))
              (if (null? found)
                  (string-append n " is not defined")
                  (tagcase (car found)
                    (bind (n2 sc w)
                      (tagcase sc
                        (scheme (tvars t)
                          (string-append n (string-append " : " (string-append (show-ty (new-state) t) (if (string=? w "prim") ", a primitive" "")))))))))))))

      (define* f-loaded! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f path now)
            "`,load FILE`: the file's forms, one entry."
            (tagcase (the (sumof (data (bytevectorof r)) (failed io-error)) (read-file path))
              (data b (tagcase (utf8->string b)
                        (text t (f-submit! f t path #f now))
                        (bad k (f-said! f (string-append path ": not UTF-8") now))))
              (failed e (f-said! f (string-append "cannot read " (string-append path (string-append ": " (extract e detail)))) now))))))

      (define* f-pending-text (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            (let ((open (f-unfinished (f-oldest-first (get (extract f entries)) nil))))
              (if (null? open)
                  "no entry is running"
                  (words-lines (f-pending-lines open)))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-pending-lines (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff spin (read @globals)) ((listof (fentry r) acyclic)) strings))
          (lambda (es)
            (if (null? es)
                nil
                (cons (string-append "[" (string-append (i64->string (extract (car es) num)) (string-append "] " (first-line (extract (car es) text)))))
                      (f-pending-lines (cdr es)))))))

      (define* f-command! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f line now)
            (let* ((w (command-word line)) (rest (trimmed-end (command-rest line))))
              (cond ((string=? w ",help")
                     (if (string=? rest "") (f-said! f help-text now) (f-said! f (f-described f rest) now)))
                    ((string=? w ",type") (f-typed-only! f rest now))
                    ((string=? w ",time") (f-submit! f rest "" #t now))
                    ((string=? w ",load") (f-loaded! f rest now))
                    ((string=? w ",pending") (f-said! f (f-pending-text f now) now))
                    ((string=? w ",cancel")
                     (let ((found (f-numbered (get (extract f entries)) (number-from (string-chars rest) 0))))
                       (if (and (not (null? found)) (f-unfinished? (car found)))
                           (f-asked! f (cancel-asked (extract (car found) num)))
                           (f-said! f (string-append "no entry " (string-append rest " is running")) now))))
                    ((string=? w ",step-limit")
                     (begin
                       (cond ((string=? rest "none") (set (extract f step-limit) -1))
                             ((string=? rest "") #u)
                             (else (set (extract f step-limit) (number-from (string-chars rest) 0))))
                       (f-asked! f (limit-asked (get (extract f step-limit))))
                       (f-said! f (if (i64< (get (extract f step-limit)) 0) "no step limit" (string-append "an entry may take " (string-append (i64->string (get (extract f step-limit))) " steps"))) now)))
                    ((string=? w ",apropos")
                     (f-said! f (let ((found (sorted-strings (deduped-names (concat (map (lambda ((n string)) (if (i64>= (int->i64 (string-search n rest 0)) 0) (list n) nil)) (f-known-names f))) nil))))
                                  (if (null? found) "nothing" (words-of-at-most found 40)))
                              now))
                    ((string=? w ",quit") (set (extract f quitting) #t))
                    (else (f-said! f (string-append "no command " (string-append w "; ,help for those there are")) now)))))))

      (define* f-interrupt! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            "^C: the draft dropped, if there is one; else the newest entry not
             ended, interrupted."
            (if (not (string=? (get (extract f draft)) ""))
                (begin (f-draft-set! f "" 0) (set (extract f history-at) -1))
                (let ((running (f-unfinished (get (extract f entries)))))
                  (if (null? running)
                      (set (extract f leaving) #f)
                      (f-asked! f (cancel-asked (extract (car running) num)))))))))

      (define* f-entered! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            "Enter: the draft given, if whole (a command's line, or forms); else a
             newline where the cursor is."
            (let* ((d (get (extract f draft)))
                   (trimmed (trimmed-start (string-chars d))))
              (cond ((and (not (null? trimmed)) (char=? (car trimmed) #\,) (command-whole? (list->string trimmed)))
                     (begin (f-given! f d now) (f-command! f (list->string trimmed) now)))
                    ((repl-complete? d) (begin (f-given! f d now) (f-submit! f d "" #f now)))
                    ((null? trimmed) (f-draft-set! f "" 0))
                    (else (f-inserted! f "\n")))))))

      (define* f-key! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) i64 i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f c now)
            "One key: typed, an editing key, or part of an escape sequence (ESC
             `[` digits and a final key: the arrows, Home, End, Delete)."
            (let ((d (get (extract f draft))) (at (get (extract f cursor))))
              (cond ((i64= (get (extract f escape)) 1)
                     (if (or (i64= c 91) (i64= c 79)) (begin (set (extract f escape) 2) (set (extract f escape-param) 0)) (set (extract f escape) 0)))
                    ((i64= (get (extract f escape)) 2)
                     (if (and (i64>= c 48) (i64<= c 57))
                         (set (extract f escape-param) (i64+ (i64* (get (extract f escape-param)) 10) (i64- c 48)))
                         (begin (set (extract f escape) 0) (f-escaped! f c now))))
                    ((i64= c 27) (set (extract f escape) 1))
                    ((i64= c 3) (f-interrupt! f now))
                    ((i64= c 4) (if (string=? d "") (set (extract f leaving) #t) (f-deleted! f at (i64+ at 1))))
                    ((or (i64= c 127) (i64= c 8)) (f-deleted! f (i64- at 1) at))
                    ((or (i64= c 13) (i64= c 10)) (f-entered! f now))
                    ((i64= c 1) (f-moved! f (line-start d at)))
                    ((i64= c 5) (f-moved! f (line-end d at)))
                    ((i64= c 2) (f-moved! f (i64- at 1)))
                    ((i64= c 6) (f-moved! f (i64+ at 1)))
                    ((i64= c 11)
                     (let ((e (line-end d at)))
                       (f-deleted! f at (if (i64= e at) (i64+ e 1) e))))
                    ((i64= c 21) (f-deleted! f (line-start d at) at))
                    ((i64= c 23) (f-deleted! f (word-start d at) at))
                    ((i64= c 16) (f-history-moved! f 1))
                    ((i64= c 14) (f-history-moved! f -1))
                    ((i64= c 9) (f-completed! f now))
                    ((i64= c 12)
                     (begin (f-say! f "\x1b;[H\x1b;[2J") (set (extract f rows) (i64+ (get (extract f rows)) (get (extract f screen-rows))))
                            (set (extract f cursor-row) 0) (set (extract f draft-dirty) #t)))
                    ((i64< c 32) #u)
                    (else (f-inserted! f (char->string (integer->char (i64->int c))))))))))


      "Speculation (C96, C97): the draft checked as it is typed, each try a
       worker's, as C103's session did it."

      (define* f-holes-set! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) string i64 (listof i64 acyclic)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f text kept open)
            "The draft with a hole where the next item of its innermost open list
             goes: closed, and with a filler after the hole in each list around it,
             so that a form missing its later parts still reaches the hole; and
             what the hole is in that list, read by a worker. None if no list is
             open, or it is quoted data."
            (if (or (null? open) (quoted-at? text (car open)))
                (begin (set (extract f hole-texts) nil) (set (extract f hole-at) -1))
                (let ((typed (trimmed-end (cut text 0 kept))))
                  (begin
                    ;; Bare; a filler after the hole in every list; in one list around it alone.
                    (set (extract f hole-texts)
                         (cons (string-append typed (string-append " %hole" (closers (size open))))
                               (cons (string-append typed (string-append " %hole" (closers-filled 0 (size open) -1)))
                                     (each-filled (string-append typed " %hole") 1 (size open)))))
                    (set (extract f hole-at) (i64+ (string-length-i64 typed) 1))
                    (tagcase (worked (hole-items (string-append (cut text (car open) kept) ")")))
                      (items-done (n op) (begin (set (extract f hole-place) n) (set (extract f hole-op) op)))
                      (else other (begin (set (extract f hole-place) 0) (set (extract f hole-op) ""))))))))))

      (define* f-hint-words (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string string) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f what argument)
            "What the hole wants, as the note says it: a call's `argument` (`argument
             2`, if the checker said it is one), with its operator if a name; else
             what goes next."
            (let ((want "an expression of type ") (op (get (extract f hole-op))))
              (cond ((and (has-prefix? what want) (not (string=? argument "")))
                     (string-append argument (string-append (if (string=? op "") "" (string-append " of " op))
                                                            (string-append " wants " (cut what (string-length-i64 want) (string-length-i64 what))))))
                    ((and (string=? what "an expression") (not (string=? argument "")))
                     (string-append argument (if (string=? op "") ": anything" (string-append " of " (string-append op ": anything")))))
                    ((and (has-prefix? what "nothing, the call has its ") (not (string=? op "")))
                     (string-append op (string-append " takes " (cut what 26 (string-length-i64 what)))))
                    ;; An operator could be anything; saying so says nothing.
                    ((and (string=? what "an expression") (i64= (get (extract f hole-place)) 0)) "")
                    (else (string-append "next: " what)))))))

      (define* f-hints-said! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r)) ((fstate r)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            "No hole reached: the narrowest refusal of a list around it, if any,
             says what that list must be."
            (begin
              (set (extract f spec-phase) 4)
              (if (string=? (get (extract f around)) "") #u (f-noted! f (string-append "next: " (get (extract f around))) #f))))))

      (define* f-expression-speculated! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string strings (listof i64 acyclic)) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f type effects named)
            (let ((waiting (f-unfinished-of (get (extract f entries)) named)))
              (begin
                (set (extract f spec-type) type)
                (cond ((not (null? waiting))
                       (begin
                         (set (extract f spec-waits) #t)
                         (f-noted! f (string-append "…" (string-append type (string-append "  (run when [" (string-append (i64->string (car waiting)) "] has ended)")))) #f)))
                      ((not (quiet-effect? effects))
                       (f-noted! f (string-append "…" (string-append type (string-append "  (not run early, for its " (string-append (show-effs (loud-atoms effects)) ")")))) #f))
                      (else
                       (begin
                         (set (extract f spec-serial) (i64+ (get (extract f spec-serial)) 1))
                         (f-asked! f (draft-asked (get (extract f spec-serial)) (get (extract f spec-text)) type))
                         (set (extract f spec-state) 1)
                         (f-noted! f (string-append "…" type) #f)))))))))

      (define* f-speculation-refused! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) string i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f message now)
            "A try refused (its worker failed). The draft as it is: said, its
             subform underlined, if it is about what has been finished. With a
             hole: what goes there, if the checker reached it; else, if about a
             list around the hole, kept if the narrowest so far."
            (let ((at (refused-offset message)) (words (refusal-words message)) (holes (get (extract f trying-holes)))
                  (kept (get (extract f spec-kept))) (open (get (extract f spec-open))))
              (begin
                (set (extract f trying-holes) #f)
                (cond ((not holes)
                       (if (or (get (extract f spec-finished))
                               (and (i64>= at 0) (i64< at kept) (not (i64-member? at open))))
                           (begin
                             (set (extract f spec-phase) 4)
                             (if (i64>= at 0)
                                 (begin (set (extract f under-from) at) (set (extract f under-to) (datum-end (get (extract f draft)) at)))
                                 #u)
                             (f-noted! f words #t))
                           #u))
                      ;; With the hole, the closing off no longer breaks the forms around
                      ;; it, so an error in a finished subform may come out now.
                      ((and (i64>= at 0) (i64< at kept) (not (i64-member? at open)))
                       (begin
                         (set (extract f spec-phase) 4)
                         (set (extract f under-from) at)
                         (set (extract f under-to) (datum-end (get (extract f draft)) at))
                         (f-noted! f words #t)))
                      ((has-prefix? words "the hole: ")
                       (begin (set (extract f spec-phase) 4) (f-noted! f (f-hint-words f (cut words 10 (string-length-i64 words)) "") #f)))
                      ;; A call's argument: `in argument K: the hole: …`.
                      ((and (has-prefix? words "in argument ") (i64>= (int->i64 (string-search words ": the hole: " 0)) 0))
                       (let ((at2 (int->i64 (string-search words ": the hole: " 0))))
                         (begin (set (extract f spec-phase) 4) (f-noted! f (f-hint-words f (cut words (i64+ at2 12) (string-length-i64 words)) (cut words 3 at2)) #f))))
                      ((and (i64-member? at open) (i64> at (get (extract f around-at)))
                            (i64< (int->i64 (string-search words "%hole" 0)) 0) (i64< (int->i64 (string-search words "%fill" 0)) 0))
                       (begin (set (extract f around) words) (set (extract f around-at) at)))
                      (else #u)))))))

      (define* f-draft-tried! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            (let* ((d (get (extract f draft)))
                   (trimmed (trimmed-start (string-chars d)))
                   (closing (if (and (not (null? trimmed)) (char=? (car trimmed) #\,)) (unclosable) (closed-text d)))
                   (key (tagcase closing
                          (unclosable () "")
                          (closed-as (closed kept open finished) (string-append (if finished "f|" "u|") (trimmed-end closed))))))
              (if (and (not (string=? key "")) (string=? key (get (extract f spec-key))))
                  (set (extract f speculated) #t)
                  (begin
                    (f-speculation-dropped! f)
                    (set (extract f speculated) #t)
                    (set (extract f spec-key) key)
                    (tagcase closing
                      (unclosable () #u)
                      (closed-as (closed kept open finished)
                        (begin
                          (set (extract f spec-text) closed)
                          (set (extract f spec-kept) kept)
                          (set (extract f spec-open) open)
                          (set (extract f spec-finished) finished)
                          (f-holes-set! f d kept open)
                          ;; Holes next, unless this is finished or refused for what is.
                          (set (extract f spec-phase) (if (or finished (null? (get (extract f hole-texts)))) 4 1))
                          ;; Checked after what the entries before it defined; if
                          ;; finished, an expression's type said, and run if it may be;
                          ;; definitions' types said.
                          (tagcase (worked (try (get (extract f cv)) (get (extract f globals)) closed finished))
                            (refused-done (m) (f-speculation-refused! f m now))
                            (tried-expression (type effects named) (f-expression-speculated! f type effects named))
                            (tried-definitions (lines) (f-noted! f lines #f))
                            (else other #u)))))))))))

      (define* f-speculate! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) i64) bool))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now)
            "The draft checked as it is typed, a try at a time, while this says
             there is another to make: checked as it is, once for each text it
             has been (and run, if finished and its effect allows); then, if a
             list is open, with a hole where its next item goes, and with
             fillers after that, until the checker says what goes there (C97).
             Not in plain mode, nor for a command's line."
            (cond ((not (get (extract f live))) #f)
                  ((not (get (extract f speculated))) (begin (f-draft-tried! f now) #t))
                  ((and (i64< (get (extract f spec-phase)) 4) (not (null? (get (extract f hole-texts)))))
                   (let ((text (car (get (extract f hole-texts)))))
                     (begin
                       (set (extract f spec-phase) 2)
                       (set (extract f hole-texts) (cdr (get (extract f hole-texts))))
                       (set (extract f trying-holes) #t)
                       (tagcase (worked (try (get (extract f cv)) (get (extract f globals)) text #f))
                         (refused-done (m) (f-speculation-refused! f m now))
                         (else other #u))
                       (set (extract f trying-holes) #f)
                       #t)))
                  ((i64< (get (extract f spec-phase)) 4) (begin (f-hints-said! f) #f))
                  (else #f)))))

      (define-rec
        (f-speculating! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
          (lambda (f now) (if (f-speculate! f now) (f-speculating! f now) #u))))

      "What the machine tells."

      (define* f-news! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) told i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f n now)
            "An entry's state, line and output; the draft's run's outcome, if
             that run is still the draft's."
            (tagcase n
              (entry-told (k state shown out began ended steps collected)
                (let ((found (f-numbered (get (extract f entries)) k)))
                  (if (null? found)
                      #u
                      (let ((e (car found)))
                        (begin
                          (set (extract e shown) shown)
                          (set (extract e out) (string-append (get (extract e out)) out))
                          (set (extract e began) began)
                          (set (extract e steps) steps)
                          (set (extract e collected) collected)
                          (if (and (f-unfinished? e) (not (i64<= state st-running)))
                              (f-ended! f e state ended)
                              (set (extract e state) state)))))))
              (draft-told (serial text error)
                (if (and (i64= serial (get (extract f spec-serial))) (i64= (get (extract f spec-state)) 1))
                    (begin (set (extract f spec-state) 2) (f-noted! f text error))
                    #u))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-each-news! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (read @globals) spin) ((fstate r) (listof told acyclic) i64) unit))
          (lambda (f ns now) (if (null? ns) #u (begin (f-news! f (car ns) now) (f-each-news! f (cdr ns) now))))))

      (define* f-wait-ms (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) spin) ((fstate r)) i64))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            "How long to wait for a key or news: long enough for a spinner's next
             frame if an entry is unfinished and the screen live, else until one
             comes."
            (if (and (get (extract f live)) (not (null? (f-unfinished (get (extract f entries)))))) 80 -1))))

      (define* f-over? (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) spin) ((fstate r)) bool))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f)
            "Whether to leave: ^D (or the input's end) asked, and no entry unfinished."
            (or (get (extract f quitting))
                (and (get (extract f leaving)) (null? (f-unfinished (get (extract f entries)))))))))

      (define* f-written! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read r) (write r) (alloc r) (read @globals) spin (io stdout)) ((fstate r) i64) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f now) (tagcase (write-out (f-screen! f now)) (done u #u) (failed e #u)))))

      (define* f-started! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) bool i64 i64 string) string))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f is-live height width path)
            "The session begun: the checker's environment, the history, the
             screen's size; the banner, if live."
            (let ((empty (cv nil nil nil nil "a type" nil "the REPL" 0 nil nil 0 (bempty) nil)))
              (begin
                (set (extract f cv) (with-binds empty (prim-binds empty)))
                (set (extract f history-path) path)
                (f-history-read! f)
                (set (extract f live) is-live)
                (set (extract f screen-rows) height)
                (set (extract f screen-cols) width)
                (if is-live
                    (string-append (repl-banner) "\r\n(each entry runs while you type the next, its value %k after it; ^C interrupts the newest, ,help for more)\r\n")
                    ""))))))

      "The front's state, made in its place."
      (define* f-new (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (alloc r) (read @globals) spin) ((addr relayed @m)) (fstate r)))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (relay)
            (product (note (new "")) (note-error (new #f)) (speculated (new #f)) (spec-kept (new 0))
                     (spec-open (new nil)) (spec-finished (new #f)) (spec-type (new ""))
                     (spec-state (new 0)) (spec-key (new "")) (spec-waits (new #f)) (spec-serial (new 0))
                     (spec-text (new "")) (spec-phase (new 4)) (hole-texts (new nil)) (trying-holes (new #f))
                     (hole-at (new -1)) (hole-op (new "")) (hole-place (new 0)) (around (new ""))
                     (around-at (new -1)) (under-from (new 0)) (under-to (new 0))
                     (live (new #f)) (screen-rows (new 24)) (screen-cols (new 80))
                     (entries (new nil)) (draft (new "")) (rows (new 0))
                     (draft-rows (new 0)) (draft-dirty (new #t)) (leaving (new #f)) (escape (new 0))
                     (written (new nil)) (cursor (new 0)) (cursor-row (new 0)) (escape-param (new 0))
                     (history (new nil)) (history-at (new -1)) (stash (new "")) (history-path (new ""))
                     (step-limit (new -1)) (commands (new 0)) (quitting (new #f))
                     (requests (new nil)) (cv (new (cv nil nil nil nil "a type" nil "the REPL" 0 nil nil 0 (bempty) nil))) (globals (new nil)) (count (new 0))
                     (input-ended (new #f)) (relay relay)))))

      "A key read, as the key's code, or -1 at the input's end (which asks to
       leave, as ^D does)."
      (define-type byte-read (sumof (byte u8) (eof unit) (failed io-error)))

      (define* f-byte! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) byte-read) unit))
        (plambda ((r region))
          (lambda (f b)
            (tagcase b
              (byte k (f-key! f (int->i64 (u8->int k)) (now-ms)))
              (else other (begin (set (extract f input-ended) #t) (set (extract f leaving) #t)))))))

      (define* front-failure (subr pure (string) relayed) (lambda (m) (from-front (front-failed m))))

      "A scripted session's keys: each line `MS TEXT`, TEXT's keys arriving
       at MS on a virtual clock (`\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\e`, `\\\\`, `\\xHH`
       escapes), as C103's Rust read them."
      (define-datatype arrival (arrival i64 (listof i64 acyclic)))

      (define hex-digit (subr kfx (i64) i64)
        (lambda (c)
          (cond ((and (i64>= c 48) (i64<= c 57)) (i64- c 48))
                ((and (i64>= c 97) (i64<= c 102)) (i64- c 87))
                ((and (i64>= c 65) (i64<= c 70)) (i64- c 55))
                (else -1))))

      (define-rec
        (unescaped-bytes (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (bs)
            (cond ((null? bs) nil)
                  ((and (i64= (car bs) 92) (not (null? (cdr bs))))
                   (let ((c (car (cdr bs))) (rest (cdr (cdr bs))))
                     (cond ((i64= c 110) (cons 10 (unescaped-bytes rest)))
                           ((i64= c 114) (cons 13 (unescaped-bytes rest)))
                           ((i64= c 116) (cons 9 (unescaped-bytes rest)))
                           ((i64= c 101) (cons 27 (unescaped-bytes rest)))
                           ((i64= c 92) (cons 92 (unescaped-bytes rest)))
                           ((and (i64= c 120) (not (null? rest)) (not (null? (cdr rest))))
                            (let ((hi (hex-digit (car rest))) (lo (hex-digit (car (cdr rest)))))
                              (cons (if (or (i64< hi 0) (i64< lo 0)) 63 (i64+ (i64* hi 16) lo)) (unescaped-bytes (cdr (cdr rest))))))
                           (else (cons c (unescaped-bytes rest))))))
                  (else (cons (car bs) (unescaped-bytes (cdr bs))))))))

      (define-rec
        (bytes-of (subr (maxeff kfx (read @io)) ((bytevectorof @io) i64 i64) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (bv i n) (if (i64>= i n) nil (cons (int->i64 (u8->int (bytevector-u8-ref bv (i64->int i)))) (bytes-of bv (i64+ i 1) n))))))

      (define-rec
        (split-bytes (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic) i64 (listof i64 acyclic) (listof (listof i64 acyclic) acyclic)) (listof (listof i64 acyclic) acyclic))
          (lambda (bs sep acc out)
            "Bytes split at `sep`, each piece's bytes in order; a last piece
             without one kept."
            (cond ((null? bs) (reversed-onto (if (null? acc) out (cons (reversed-onto acc nil) out)) nil))
                  ((i64= (car bs) sep) (split-bytes (cdr bs) sep nil (cons (reversed-onto acc nil) out)))
                  (else (split-bytes (cdr bs) sep (cons (car bs) acc) out))))))

      (define-rec
        (without-cr (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (bs) (cond ((null? bs) nil) ((and (null? (cdr bs)) (i64= (car bs) 13)) nil) (else (cons (car bs) (without-cr (cdr bs)))))))
        (blank? (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) bool)
          (lambda (bs) (cond ((null? bs) #t) ((or (i64= (car bs) 32) (i64= (car bs) 9) (i64= (car bs) 13)) (blank? (cdr bs))) (else #f))))
        (digits-value (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic) i64) i64)
          (lambda (bs n)
            (cond ((null? bs) n)
                  ((and (i64>= (car bs) 48) (i64<= (car bs) 57)) (digits-value (cdr bs) (i64+ (i64* n 10) (i64- (car bs) 48))))
                  (else 0))))
        (before-space (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (bs) (if (or (null? bs) (i64= (car bs) 32)) nil (cons (car bs) (before-space (cdr bs))))))
        (after-space (subr kfx ((listof i64 acyclic)) (listof i64 acyclic))
          (lambda (bs) (cond ((null? bs) nil) ((i64= (car bs) 32) (cdr bs)) (else (after-space (cdr bs)))))))

      (define-rec
        (arrivals-of (subr kfx ((listof (listof i64 acyclic) acyclic)) (listof arrival acyclic))
          (lambda (ls)
            (if (null? ls)
                nil
                (let ((l (without-cr (car ls))))
                  (if (or (blank? l) (i64= (car l) 35))
                      (arrivals-of (cdr ls))
                      (cons (arrival (digits-value (before-space l) 0) (unescaped-bytes (after-space l))) (arrivals-of (cdr ls)))))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-keys! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) (listof i64 acyclic) i64) unit))
          (lambda (f bs clock) (if (null? bs) #u (begin (f-key! f (car bs) clock) (f-keys! f (cdr bs) clock))))))

      (define-rec
        (f-arrived! (poly ((r region)) (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin fronting (read r) (write r) (alloc r)) ((fstate r) (listof arrival acyclic) i64) (listof arrival acyclic)))
          (lambda (f as clock)
            "The keys arriving by `clock`, given; those after, left."
            (if (null? as)
                nil
                (tagcase (car as)
                  (arrival (t bs)
                    (if (i64<= t clock) (begin (f-keys! f bs clock) (f-arrived! f (cdr as) clock)) as)))))))

)


    (define repl! (subr repling (string) int)
      (lambda (history)
        "A live session, if the standard input is a terminal (raw mode, its
         size, the history in `history`); else a plain one, the entries run
         one after another, each line written when it ends. The machine here,
         the relay and the front processes."
        (let* ((live (tagcase (terminal-raw) (done u #t) (else o #f)))
               ;; The terminal's size, or 24 by 80 if it says none (a new pty's is 0 by 0).
               (sized (tagcase (terminal-size) (size z (and (> (extract z rows) 0) (> (extract z columns) 0))) (else o #f)))
               (height (if sized (tagcase (terminal-size) (size z (int->i64 (extract z rows))) (else o (the i64 24))) (the i64 24)))
               (width (if sized (tagcase (terminal-size) (size z (int->i64 (extract z columns))) (else o (the i64 80))) (the i64 80)))
               (path (if live history "")))
          (begin
            (repl-start!)
            (set m-live live)
            ;; A slice at most some milliseconds, so that a request waits no longer.
            (if live (set m-slice-ns 4000000) #u)
            (let* ((relay (relay-made))
                   (front
                    (the (addr told @f)
                         (spawn-monitored relay front-failure (box told p)
                           (let ((f (the (fstate p) (f-new relay))))
                             (begin
                               (write-out (f-started! f live height width path))
                               ;; The prompt, before the first key.
                               (f-written! f 0)
                               (letrec ((drained (subr (maxeff front-loop (receive p) (read p) (write p) (alloc p)) (bool) bool)
                                          (lambda (typed)
                                            "Keys that have come, and news, each taken, until none waits."
                                            (if (and (not (get (extract f input-ended))) (stdin-ready?))
                                                (begin (f-byte! f (read-byte)) (drained #t))
                                                (pselect ((receive box) n (begin (f-news! f n (now-ms)) (drained typed)))
                                                         ((sleep-until (int->i64 0)) u typed)))))
                                        (go (subr (maxeff front-loop (receive p) (read p) (write p) (alloc p)) () unit)
                                          (lambda ()
                                            "A key, news, or a spinner's frame waited for; all that came
                                             taken; the requests sent; what was typed drawn, before the
                                             draft is checked; drawn again."
                                            (let* ((wait (f-wait-ms f))
                                                   (until (i64+ (clock) (i64* wait 1000000)))
                                                   (first (cond ((and (get (extract f input-ended)) (i64< wait 0))
                                                                 (pselect ((receive box) n (begin (f-news! f n (now-ms)) #f))))
                                                                ((get (extract f input-ended))
                                                                 (pselect ((receive box) n (begin (f-news! f n (now-ms)) #f))
                                                                          ((sleep-until until) u #f)))
                                                                ((i64< wait 0)
                                                                 (pselect ((read-byte) b (begin (f-byte! f b) #t))
                                                                          ((receive box) n (begin (f-news! f n (now-ms)) #f))))
                                                                (else
                                                                 (pselect ((read-byte) b (begin (f-byte! f b) #t))
                                                                          ((receive box) n (begin (f-news! f n (now-ms)) #f))
                                                                          ((sleep-until until) u #f)))))
                                                   (typed (drained first)))
                                              (begin
                                                (f-requests-sent! f)
                                                (if typed (f-written! f (now-ms)) #u)
                                                (f-speculating! f (now-ms))
                                                (f-requests-sent! f)
                                                (f-written! f (now-ms))
                                                (if (f-over? f)
                                                    (begin
                                                      (if (get (extract f live)) (begin (write-out "\r\n") #u) #u)
                                                      (send relay (from-front (front-ended))))
                                                    (go)))))))
                                 (go))))))))
              (begin
                (machine-live! relay front)
                (terminal-restore)
                0))))))

    (define scripted! (subr repling (string) int)
      (lambda (path)
        "`--keys FILE`: a session from a script of keys at virtual times, the
         front and the machine in step, a round at a time, so that it replays
         the same; what a terminal of 24 rows and 80 columns would be sent
         (the REPL's tests). The input ends after the last line."
        (tagcase (the (sumof (data (bytevectorof @io)) (failed io-error)) (read-file path))
          (failed e (begin (write-err (string-append "kayak-fx26: " (string-append path (string-append ": " (string-append (extract e detail) "\n"))))) 66))
          (data bv
            (let ((arrivals (arrivals-of (split-bytes (bytes-of bv 0 (int->i64 (bytevector-length bv))) 10 nil nil))))
              (begin
                (repl-start!)
                (set m-live #t)
                (let* ((relay (relay-made))
                       (front
                        (the (addr told @f)
                             (spawn-monitored relay front-failure (box told p)
                               (let ((f (the (fstate p) (f-new relay))))
                                 (begin
                                   (write-out (f-started! f #t 24 80 ""))
                                   (letrec ((go (subr (maxeff front-loop (receive p) (read p) (write p) (alloc p)) ((listof arrival acyclic) i64 bool) unit)
                                              (lambda (as clock ended)
                                                (let* ((left (f-arrived! f as clock))
                                                       (now-ended (if (and (null? left) (not ended)) (begin (set (extract f leaving) #t) #t) ended))
                                                       (reply (the (icell ran @q) (make-icell))))
                                                  (begin
                                                    (f-speculating! f clock)
                                                    (f-asked! f (round-ended clock reply))
                                                    (f-requests-sent! f)
                                                    (tagcase (icell-get reply)
                                                      (ran (news after idle)
                                                        (begin
                                                          (f-each-news! f news after)
                                                          (f-written! f after)
                                                          (if (f-over? f)
                                                              (begin (write-out "\r\n") (send relay (from-front (front-ended))))
                                                              (go left
                                                                  (cond ((not idle) after)
                                                                        ;; Nothing to run: the clock to the next key, or a frame on.
                                                                        ((null? left) (i64+ after 80))
                                                                        (else (tagcase (car left) (arrival (t bs) (if (i64> t (i64+ after 1)) t (i64+ after 1))))))
                                                                  now-ended))))))))))
                                     (go arrivals 0 #f))))))))
                  (begin
                    (machine-scripted! relay nil)
                    0))))))))))
